D('intercept',{etymology:{"origin":"Intercept entered English from Latin interceptus, the past participle of intercipere, to seize in passing, formed from inter, between, and capere, to take.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intercept entered English from Latin interceptus, the past participle of intercipere, to seize in passing, formed from inter, between, and capere, to take."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin parts convey catching something between its starting point and destination.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深的 PIE 词根不是理解本义所必需；构词解释止于可信的拉丁形式。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intercept"},contexts:[{"domain":"体育与通信","senseId":"intercept.s1","en":"The defender stepped in front of the pass and intercepted the ball before it reached the striker waiting near the goal.","zh":"防守队员抢到传球路线前方，在球到达球门附近等待的前锋之前将其截下。","structure":"and 连接防守队员的动作，before 从句说明拦截必须完成的时间点。","grammar":"intercept 后接被拦截的对象；before 引导时间状语从句。","rationale":"intercept 表示在途中拦下某物，此处具体对象是传向前锋的球。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A defender intercepted the pass before it reached the striker.','一名后卫在传球到达前锋脚下之前拦截了球。')],mistakes:[m('The goalkeeper intercepted the ball after it had already crossed the goal line and counted as a goal.','The goalkeeper intercepted the ball before it crossed the goal line.','若球已过门线并算作进球，就不能再说守门员把它拦截在途中；把时间改到越线之前。')],quiz:[q('intercept',1,1,'A guard intercepts a message. What does the guard do?','stops it before it reaches its destination','writes a reply after reading it','sends it to every recipient','intercept 强调在到达目的地前截下。'),q('intercept',2,1,'Which event is an interception in basketball?','A player catches an opponent’s pass.','A player scores after a free throw.','A player asks the referee for a timeout.','截住对手传球是拦截传球。'),q('intercept',3,1,'The aircraft was intercepted near the border. It was?','stopped or met before proceeding farther','repaired after landing','painted before takeoff','intercept 可指拦截正在前进的飞机。'),q('intercept',4,1,'Choose the correct form: They ___ the call yesterday.','intercepted','interceptted','intercepting','intercept 的过去式拼作 intercepted，只双写不需要再加 t。')]});
D('interchange',{etymology:{"origin":"Interchange came from Old French entrechangier, formed from entre-, between, and changier, to change; the noun followed from the verb.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interchange came from Old French entrechangier, formed from entre-, between, and changier, to change; the noun followed from the verb."}],"formationLogic":"The reciprocal prefix and verb together express changing or giving things to one another.","mnemonic":null,"note":"句中互换的是信息，因此采用与该词历史构词相符的相互交换义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interchange"},contexts:[{"domain":"工作协作","senseId":"interchange.s1","en":"The two research teams agreed to interchange data only after both had removed names that could identify the patients.","zh":"两支研究团队同意互换数据，但要等双方都删除可能识别患者身份的姓名之后。","structure":"only after 强调交换的先决条件，that 从句限定需删除的姓名。","grammar":"interchange 在此作及物动词，data 作交换对象。","rationale":"interchange 表示双方相互交换信息，匿名处理是交换前的具体约束。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The two drivers agreed to interchange their shifts next week.','两位司机同意下周互换班次。')],mistakes:[m('At the interchange, the two highways crossed, but neither road connected to the other.','At the interchange, the two highways crossed and connected to the other.','公路 interchange 是道路交会并可转换路线的枢纽；说两路互不连接与此处交通枢纽义冲突。')],quiz:[q('interchange',1,1,'At a highway interchange, drivers can usually?','move from one road to another','exchange their car engines','stop all traffic permanently','公路 interchange 是道路互通的立交枢纽。'),q('interchange',2,1,'The teams interchanged seats. What happened?','They swapped seats with each other.','They removed every seat.','They sat in the same seat at once.','interchange 作动词可表示互换位置。'),q('interchange',3,1,'An interchange of ideas involves people?','sharing ideas with one another','keeping every idea secret','counting the pages in a book','interchange 也可指想法或信息的交流交换。'),q('interchange',4,1,'Which phrase describes a road junction with connecting ramps?','a highway interchange','a highway interview','a highway interval','interchange 可指高速公路互通立交。')]});
D('intercourse',{etymology:{"origin":"Intercourse came from Old French entrecors, exchange, commerce, or communication, from Late Latin intercursus, a running between, based on intercurrere.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intercourse came from Old French entrecors, exchange, commerce, or communication, from Late Latin intercursus, a running between, based on intercurrere."}],"formationLogic":"The original idea of movement between parties developed into trade and social communication; the sexual sense is later.","mnemonic":null,"note":"本句锁定普通交流义，避免把现代常见性义泛化到所有场景。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intercourse"},contexts:[{"domain":"国际贸易史","senseId":"intercourse.s1","en":"For centuries, commercial intercourse between the port and inland villages depended on traders who carried news as well as salt and cloth.","zh":"几个世纪以来，港口与内陆村庄之间的商业往来依靠商人，他们不仅运送盐和布匹，也传递消息。","structure":"between 引出往来的双方，who 从句补充 traders 所做的事情。","grammar":"commercial 修饰 intercourse；as well as 连接货物与信息两项内容。","rationale":"intercourse 的此处义是群体间持续的交流与往来，不是性行为义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Regular commercial intercourse linked the port with inland towns.','定期的商业往来把港口和内陆城镇联系起来。'),ex(2,'The leaflet explains how to reduce the risk of infection during sexual intercourse.','这份宣传单说明如何降低性交时感染的风险。')],mistakes:[m('The history describes sexual intercourse between two cities as trade and diplomacy.','The history describes social intercourse between two cities as trade and diplomacy.','sexual 明确指性行为，不能表示两座城市间的贸易与外交往来；这里应改为 social。')],quiz:[q('intercourse',1,1,'In the formal phrase social intercourse, the word means?','dealings and communication between people','a short break in a performance','an argument over a legal contract','social intercourse 是人与人之间的交往往来。'),q('intercourse',2,2,'In a medical text, sexual intercourse refers to?','sexual activity between people','a business meeting between companies','a conversation about a school subject','sexual intercourse 是性行为这一医学表达。'),q('intercourse',3,1,'Why might a writer say commercial intercourse between ports?','to describe trade and contact between them','to describe a private medical examination','to describe a pause between ships','商业往来义较正式，指群体或地区之间的交往。'),q('intercourse',4,2,'Which context most clearly signals the sexual sense?','a clinic discussing contraception and sexual intercourse','a history of trade between ancient cities','a report on diplomatic communication','clinic 与 contraception 的上下文表明这里指性行为。')]});
D('interest',{etymology:{"origin":"Interest passed through Old French interest from Latin interest, literally it is important or it makes a difference, a form of interresse, to concern; its path to profit and financial senses is not entirely clear.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interest passed through Old French interest from Latin interest, literally it is important or it makes a difference, a form of interresse, to concern; its path to profit and financial senses is not entirely clear."}],"formationLogic":"The financial noun developed historically from notions of concern, compensation, and benefit, though the exact semantic transition is uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 对从利益到金融利息的意义演变说明并不完全确定。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interest"},contexts:[{"domain":"个人理财","senseId":"interest.s4","en":"Because the account pays interest monthly, the balance grew even in months when Lina made no additional deposit.","zh":"由于账户每月支付利息，即使莉娜在某些月份没有继续存钱，余额也会增长。","structure":"because 从句解释余额增长的原因，when 从句限定没有存款的月份。","grammar":"interest 作不可数名词，指借用资金所支付的钱；pay interest 是金融搭配。","rationale":"这里 interest 明确是存款利息，而非兴趣或利益。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She takes a strong interest in local history.','她对当地历史很感兴趣。'),ex(2,'Cycling is one of his main interests.','骑行是他的主要爱好之一。'),ex(3,'The new timetable is in the interest of passengers who need an early connection.','新时刻表符合需要赶早班接驳的乘客的利益。'),ex(4,'The loan charges interest only after the first six months.','这笔贷款只在头六个月之后收取利息。'),ex(5,'She bought a controlling interest in the family business.','她买下了这家家族企业的控股权益。'),ex(6,'May I interest you in a seat near the window?','要不要坐靠窗的座位？')],mistakes:[m('The bank paid five percent interests on the savings account each year.','The bank paid five percent interest on the savings account each year.','表示存款收益率时 interest 通常不可数；这里不加复数词尾。')],quiz:[q('interest',1,1,'If a science book holds a child’s interest, the child?','wants to keep reading or learning','must pay the book’s loan charge','owns part of the publisher','hold someone’s interest 是持续吸引其注意。'),q('interest',2,3,'A decision made in the public interest is made for?','the benefit of the community','the bank’s monthly loan payment','the entertainment value of a hobby','in the public interest 指为了公众利益。'),q('interest',3,4,'A bank charges interest on a loan. What is interest here?','money paid for borrowing money','a hobby the borrower enjoys','a share of the bank’s ownership','金融语境的 interest 是借款利息。'),q('interest',4,5,'An investor’s interest in a company can mean?','a share or stake in its ownership','curiosity about its office building','the fee paid on a personal loan','interest 可指企业或财产中的权益、股份。')]});
D('interface',{etymology:{"origin":"Interface was formed in the nineteenth century from inter- and face for a common boundary; later computing senses describe a place or device where systems interact.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interface was formed in the nineteenth century from inter- and face for a common boundary; later computing senses describe a place or device where systems interact."}],"formationLogic":"The shared-boundary image extended naturally to the point through which a user and a computer exchange actions or information.","mnemonic":null,"note":"早期边界义与后来的交互义应区分；此处语境取软件界面。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interface"},contexts:[{"domain":"软件设计","senseId":"interface.s1","en":"The revised interface places the search box beside the results, so users can compare two definitions without leaving the page.","zh":"改版后的界面把搜索框放在结果旁边，因此用户无需离开页面就能比较两个释义。","structure":"so 引出布局带来的结果，without leaving 限制比较操作所需的步骤。","grammar":"interface 作名词指系统之间供人操作或互动的界面；can compare 表示能力。","rationale":"此处指软件使用者看到并操作的界面，是两个系统或用户与系统的交互面。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The app has a simple interface that lets users change the language.','这款应用的界面简洁，用户可以在其中切换语言。')],mistakes:[m('The new interface connects the user with the software, but users cannot see or operate any controls on it.','The new interface connects the user with the software and provides controls they can operate.','用户界面是人与软件交互的表面；既无法看到也无法操作任何控件，就不能起界面作用。')],quiz:[q('interface',1,1,'A user interface is the part of a system that?','lets a person interact with it','stores electricity in a battery','prints every document automatically','interface 可指用户与系统互动的界面。'),q('interface',2,1,'A hardware interface allows two devices to?','connect or communicate with each other','become the same physical object','avoid exchanging any signals','interface 也可指系统或设备之间的连接界面。'),q('interface',3,1,'If two departments interface closely, they?','work or communicate with each other','are physically separated by a wall','stop sharing information entirely','interface 作动词可表示相互配合或连接。'),q('interface',4,1,'Which detail is most likely part of a website interface?','the buttons and menus visitors use','the electricity bill for the office','the private thoughts of its designer','按钮和菜单属于用户可操作的界面元素。')]});
D('interfere',{etymology:{"origin":"Interfere came through Old French enterferer, to exchange blows or strike one another, from entre-, between, and ferir, to strike.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interfere came through Old French enterferer, to exchange blows or strike one another, from entre-, between, and ferir, to strike."}],"formationLogic":"The physical idea of striking or mixing between things developed figuratively into obstructing or disrupting a process.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源中 PIE 远源有重建争议；此处仅采用古法语和拉丁语阶段。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interfere"},contexts:[{"domain":"无线通信","senseId":"interfere.s2","en":"A nearby transmitter can interfere with the emergency radio signal, making the dispatcher’s instructions difficult for the rescue team to hear.","zh":"附近的发射器可能干扰应急无线电信号，使救援队难以听清调度员的指示。","structure":"making 分词短语说明信号受干扰产生的后果。","grammar":"interfere with something 是固定搭配；make + object + adjective 表示使某物处于某状态。","rationale":"interfere 在此表示妨碍设备正常工作，符合词条的阻碍义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The editor refused to interfere in the author’s choice of subject.','编辑拒绝干涉作者对题材的选择。'),ex(2,'A metal cover may interfere with the radio signal.','金属罩可能会干扰无线电信号。')],mistakes:[m('The constant alerts interfered with her concentration, helping her finish the report sooner.','The constant alerts interfered with her concentration, making it harder to finish the report.','干扰注意力会妨碍而不是帮助顺利完成报告；将结果改为更难完成。')],quiz:[q('interfere',1,1,'To interfere in a private disagreement is to?','get involved when your involvement is unwanted','quietly record the disagreement for later','leave both people alone','interfere in 常表示插手他人的事务。'),q('interfere',2,2,'A loud fan interferes with a recording when it?','makes the recording harder to hear clearly','improves the sound quality','translates the recording into another language','interfere with 表示妨碍某事正常进行。'),q('interfere',3,1,'Which preposition fits the meaning “meddle in their affairs”?','in','to','from','interfere in affairs 表示干涉事务。'),q('interfere',4,2,'Which sentence uses interfere with naturally?','The walls interfere with the wireless signal.','The walls interfere at the wireless signal.','The walls interfere the wireless signal.','表示干扰某物时用 interfere with，不能直接接宾语。')]});
D('interfere with',{etymology:{"origin":"Interfere with combines interfere, from Old French enterferer, with the preposition with to mark the process or object obstructed.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interfere with combines interfere, from Old French enterferer, with the preposition with to mark the process or object obstructed."}],"formationLogic":"The phrase uses the verb’s established meddling or obstruction sense with an explicit target.","mnemonic":null,"note":"短语的来源说明依赖 interfere 的可核实历史和现代搭配。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interfere"},contexts:[{"domain":"设备维护","senseId":"interfere with.s1","en":"Do not interfere with the cooling fan while the machine is running, because touching the blades could stop the airflow and damage the motor.","zh":"机器运行时不要碰动冷却风扇，因为触碰叶片可能会阻断气流并损坏电机。","structure":"because 从句解释警告原因，while 从句限定禁止操作的时段。","grammar":"interfere with 后接受干扰对象；could stop 与 damage 并列。","rationale":"interfere with 表示妨碍设备正常工作，句中的触碰会破坏风扇功能。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The magnetic field can interfere with the compass reading.','磁场可能干扰罗盘的读数。')],mistakes:[m('The thick walls interfered with the signal, so the reception became perfectly clear.','The thick walls interfered with the signal, so the reception became weak.','信号受干扰通常使接收变差；改成 weak 与前因相符。')],quiz:[q('interfere with',1,1,'A device interferes with a radio signal if it?','disrupts or weakens the signal','stores the signal safely','translates it into written text','interfere with 可表示干扰信号。'),q('interfere with',2,1,'If a medicine interferes with another treatment, it may?','affect how that treatment works','make the treatment a type of food','prove that no treatment was given','短语表示对治疗效果产生干扰影响。'),q('interfere with',3,1,'Choose the correct construction.','Do not interfere with the controls.','Do not interfere to the controls.','Do not interfere the controls.','该短语中的 with 不能省略或替换为 to。'),q('interfere with',4,1,'What does “The delay interfered with our plans” mean?','The delay disrupted our plans.','The delay improved our plans.','The delay explained our plans.','interfere with plans 表示打乱或妨碍计划。')]});
D('interference',{etymology:{"origin":"Interference, first recorded in 1783 as meddling, was formed from interfere on the model of difference; its wave-physics sense came later.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interference, first recorded in 1783 as meddling, was formed from interfere on the model of difference; its wave-physics sense came later."}],"formationLogic":"The general noun first named unwanted meddling and was later applied to interacting waves and noisy signals.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处采用音频噪声义；词源依据该名词由 interfere 派生。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interference"},contexts:[{"domain":"音频技术","senseId":"interference.s1","en":"The recording contains interference from a faulty cable, so the editor replaced it before mixing the interview with the background music.","zh":"录音中有故障电缆带来的杂音，因此编辑在把访谈与背景音乐混音前更换了电缆。","structure":"so 引出处理结果，before 从句说明更换发生在混音之前。","grammar":"interference 作不可数名词指不需要的噪声；it 回指 cable。","rationale":"这里的 interference 是录音信号中的杂音，而不是人插手他人事务。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The pilot reported radio interference during the storm.','飞行员报告暴风雨期间出现无线电干扰。')],mistakes:[m('The referee was praised for interference because he stayed out of the players’ dispute.','The referee was praised for his lack of interference because he stayed out of the players’ dispute.','interference 指干预或干扰；保持不插手应说 lack of interference。')],quiz:[q('interference',1,1,'Radio interference is unwanted?','noise or disturbance in a signal','a new radio station license','a clear improvement in reception','无线电 interference 是信号受到的干扰。'),q('interference',2,1,'A complaint about political interference usually concerns?','unwanted involvement in another body’s decisions','a broken microphone cable','a scheduled pause in a meeting','政治干预是对他方决策的不当插手。'),q('interference',3,1,'Which phrase is natural for signal disruption?','electrical interference','electrical interest','electrical interval','electrical interference 是电气干扰。'),q('interference',4,1,'The manager denied interference in the investigation. The manager denied?','meddling in how it was conducted','paying interest on its budget','taking a break during it','这里 interference 指插手调查过程。')]});
D('interim',{etymology:{"origin":"Interim came from Latin interim, meanwhile or in the midst of that; as an adjective it means belonging to an intervening period and is recorded around 1600.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interim came from Latin interim, meanwhile or in the midst of that; as an adjective it means belonging to an intervening period and is recorded around 1600."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin time adverb became an adjective for something serving during the interval before a permanent arrangement.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源按 Etymonline 的 interim 词条说明，不额外拆分 im。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interim"},contexts:[{"domain":"项目管理","senseId":"interim.s1","en":"An interim director will oversee the department until the board completes its search and appoints a permanent replacement.","zh":"董事会完成遴选并任命长期继任者之前，一位临时主任将负责管理该部门。","structure":"until 从句给出临时任职结束的条件，and 连接董事会的两项后续工作。","grammar":"interim 作定语修饰 director；will oversee 表示未来职责。","rationale":"interim 表示仅在正式安排就绪前持续的暂时状态。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'An interim director will lead the team until a permanent director is appointed.','在正式任命常任主任之前，由一位临时主任带领团队。'),ex(2,'The new bridge should open next spring; in the interim, buses will use the old route.','新桥预计明年春天开放；在此期间，公交车将继续走旧路线。')],mistakes:[m('The interim director was appointed permanently for only three weeks until the permanent director arrived.','The interim director was appointed temporarily for three weeks until the permanent director arrived.','interim 表示过渡或临时安排，与 permanent 永久任命矛盾；改为 temporarily。')],quiz:[q('interim',1,1,'An interim agreement is intended to last?','until a final agreement is ready','forever without any review','only for the past few years','interim 强调在正式或最终安排之前暂时有效。'),q('interim',2,2,'In the interim, the team waited for approval. When did it wait?','during the period before approval','after the project had ended','before the application was submitted','in the interim 指两件事之间的过渡时期。'),q('interim',3,1,'Which job title is a temporary replacement?','interim chair','permanent chair','retired chair','interim chair 是临时主持人或主席。'),q('interim',4,2,'Which sentence uses interim as a noun phrase?','In the interim, keep the receipts.','The interim report arrived.','They will interim the report.','in the interim 是名词短语，意为在此期间。')]});
D('interior',{etymology:{"origin":"Interior came from Latin interior, inner or middle, the comparative form of inter, within; the noun later named an inside part or inland region.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interior came from Latin interior, inner or middle, the comparative form of inter, within; the noun later named an inside part or inland region."}],"formationLogic":"The comparative adjective meaning further within developed into a noun for the inside of a bounded place.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁比较级的构词关系受词源词典支持。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interior"},contexts:[{"domain":"建筑空间","senseId":"interior.s1","en":"A narrow hallway connects the bright courtyard with the dark interior of the old house, where several rooms still have wooden ceilings.","zh":"一条狭长走廊把明亮的庭院与老房子的昏暗内部相连，里面几间屋子仍保留着木质天花板。","structure":"where 从句补充说明房屋内部的房间特点。","grammar":"interior 作名词指内部空间；connect A with B 表示连接两个地点。","rationale":"本例采用 interior 的里面部分义，而非国家内陆或室内装饰义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The expedition crossed the desert and reached the interior of the country.','探险队穿越沙漠，抵达该国内陆地区。'),ex(4,'The minister addressed several urgent interior policy questions.','部长处理了几个紧迫的内政问题。')],mistakes:[m('The interior of the country lies along its coastline, far from the inland region.','The interior of the country lies inland, far from its coastline.','interior 作名词指远离海岸的内陆；把它说成沿海与 inland 含义冲突。')],quiz:[q('interior',1,1,'The interior of a car includes?','the space inside the car','the road outside the car','the engine factory’s annual report','interior 可指物体或建筑内部空间。'),q('interior',2,2,'A journey into the interior of an island goes?','toward its inland central region','along the open sea beyond it','back to the mainland airport','the interior of a country/island 指内陆。'),q('interior',3,3,'Interior design concerns the arrangement of?','the inside spaces of buildings','the national border posts','the outside of a ship at sea','interior design 是室内设计。'),q('interior',4,4,'An interior ministry generally handles?','domestic affairs within the country','trade between planets','the decoration of private homes','political interior 可指国内事务、内政。')]});
D('interlace',{etymology:{"origin":"Interlace came through Old French entrelacier, from entre-, between, and lacier, to tie or entangle, related to lace.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interlace came through Old French entrelacier, from entre-, between, and lacier, to tie or entangle, related to lace."}],"formationLogic":"The prefix and verb together described binding crossing strands together; the modern verb preserves that weaving image.","mnemonic":null,"note":"lace 的更远来源存在争论，这里只写古法语构词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interlace"},contexts:[{"domain":"手工编织","senseId":"interlace.s1","en":"The craft worker interlaced strips of willow around the frame, tightening each row so the basket would hold its shape when lifted.","zh":"手工艺人把柳条交错编进框架，并逐行收紧，使篮子提起时仍能保持形状。","structure":"so 从句表达编织的目的，when 从句说明提篮子的情境。","grammar":"interlace + strips + around 描述交织路径；would hold 表示预期结果。","rationale":"interlace 指把多条材料交叉编在一起，柳条逐行绕框正是该动作。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The artist interlaced thin strips of paper to make a small basket.','艺术家把细纸条交织起来，编成一只小篮子。')],mistakes:[m('She interlaced the ribbons by laying them in separate parallel rows that never crossed.','She arranged the ribbons in separate parallel rows that never crossed.','interlace 表示交错编织；互不交叉的平行排列不符合这个动作，应换成 arrange。')],quiz:[q('interlace',1,1,'When two threads interlace, they?','cross and weave through each other','remain far apart','change into metal wires','interlace 表示交织、相互穿插。'),q('interlace',2,1,'Which object is most likely interlaced?','strips woven into a basket','stones scattered across a field','a sealed glass bottle','篮子编织时纸条或藤条彼此交织。'),q('interlace',3,1,'The branches interlaced above the path. They?','crossed and intertwined','grew in separate rooms','were cut into equal pieces','枝条 interlace 是彼此交错缠绕。'),q('interlace',4,1,'Choose the correct form: Their fingers were ___.','interlaced','interlacingly','interlaceded','interlaced 是 interlace 的过去分词形式。')]});
D('intermediate',{etymology:{"origin":"Intermediate came from Medieval Latin intermediatus, lying between, from Latin inter, between, and medius, middle.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intermediate came from Medieval Latin intermediatus, lying between, from Latin inter, between, and medius, middle."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin parts yield the sense of occupying a level between basic and advanced stages.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处选择语言程度义，但词源说明同时解释其核心居中概念。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intermediate"},contexts:[{"domain":"语言学习","senseId":"intermediate.s2","en":"After completing the basic course, students entered an intermediate class where they could discuss familiar topics but still practiced complex verb forms.","zh":"完成基础课程后，学生进入中级班，在那里他们可以讨论熟悉的话题，但仍需练习复杂动词形式。","structure":"after 短语说明课程顺序，where 从句补充中级班的学习特点。","grammar":"intermediate 作定语修饰 class；but 表示已掌握内容与仍需练习内容的对照。","rationale":"intermediate 表示高于基础但尚未达到高级水平，语境中展示了这种中间阶段。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'An intermediate checkpoint lies between the village and the summit.','村庄和山顶之间设有一个中间检查点。'),ex(3,'The workbook is designed for intermediates who already know basic grammar.','这本练习册面向已经掌握基础语法的中级学习者。')],mistakes:[m('The course is intermediate, designed for students who have never studied the subject before.','The course is introductory, designed for students who have never studied the subject before.','从未学过该科目的学生通常适合入门课，而 intermediate 指已超过基础阶段。')],quiz:[q('intermediate',1,1,'An intermediate stage occurs?','between an earlier and a later stage','before anything begins','only after the final result','intermediate 可形容位于两阶段之间的。'),q('intermediate',2,2,'An intermediate language course is for learners who?','know the basics but are not advanced','have never encountered the language','already teach expert-level linguistics','intermediate 水平高于初级、低于高级。'),q('intermediate',3,3,'A class for intermediates is intended for?','learners at a middle level','complete beginners only','teachers who have retired','intermediates 作名词指中级学习者。'),q('intermediate',4,1,'Which is the usual level sequence?','beginner, intermediate, advanced','advanced, beginner, intermediate','intermediate, advanced, beginner','常见课程顺序是初级、中级、高级。')]});
D('intermission',{etymology:{"origin":"Intermission came from Latin intermissionem, a breaking off or temporary pause, from intermittere, to leave an interval, formed with inter and mittere, to send or let go.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intermission came from Latin intermissionem, a breaking off or temporary pause, from intermittere, to leave an interval, formed with inter and mittere, to send or let go."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin compound described a temporary stopping point; English later used it specifically for breaks in performances.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源承认早期暂停义先于现代演出场间休息的专门用法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intermission"},contexts:[{"domain":"演出安排","senseId":"intermission.s1","en":"During the intermission, the audience left the hall for refreshments while the stage crew changed the scenery behind the closed curtain.","zh":"中场休息时，观众离开大厅去买饮料，舞台工作人员则在关闭的帷幕后更换布景。","structure":"while 连接观众和工作人员在休息时同时进行的活动。","grammar":"during 后接名词 intermission；while 从句使用过去时描述同步动作。","rationale":"intermission 是演出中间的短暂休息，布景更换解释了这段停顿的用途。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'During the intermission, the audience stretched their legs in the lobby.','中场休息时，观众在大厅里活动了一下。')],mistakes:[m('The orchestra played continuously with no break, but the program announced a long intermission.','The orchestra paused for a long intermission, as the program announced.','intermission 是演出中的休息间隔；若演奏从未停顿，就与所说的长休息矛盾。')],quiz:[q('intermission',1,1,'An intermission at a theater is?','a break between parts of a performance','the final scene of the play','a rehearsal before the audience arrives','intermission 是演出中途的休息时间。'),q('intermission',2,1,'When would audience members buy refreshments?','during the intermission','during the actors’ final bow only','after entering the theater but before the show','观众常在幕间休息时购买饮料。'),q('intermission',3,1,'A concert with an intermission has?','a pause before it continues','no music at any point','two different ticket offices','演出会暂停一段时间，然后继续。'),q('intermission',4,1,'Which word is closest in meaning in a theater program?','interval','entrance','encore','英式剧场语境中 interval 与 intermission 同指幕间休息。')]});
D('intermittent',{etymology:{"origin":"Intermittent comes from Latin intermittentem, the present participle of intermittere, to leave off, cease, or pause.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intermittent comes from Latin intermittentem, the present participle of intermittere, to leave off, cease, or pause."}],"formationLogic":"The participial adjective describes an event that repeatedly stops and resumes.","mnemonic":null,"note":"来源链关联 intermission，但词形来自拉丁现在分词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intermittent"},contexts:[{"domain":"供电与工程","senseId":"intermittent.s1","en":"Intermittent power cuts forced the clinic to move vaccine storage to a backup refrigerator that stayed cold even when the main supply failed.","zh":"断断续续的停电迫使诊所把疫苗转移到备用冰箱，即使主电源故障，它也能保持低温。","structure":"that 从句修饰备用冰箱，even when 从句强调备用设备的作用条件。","grammar":"intermittent 前置修饰 power cuts；force + object + to-infinitive 表示迫使采取行动。","rationale":"intermittent 表示发生一阵、停一阵、不连续，停电反复出现正符合该义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Intermittent rain delayed the outdoor ceremony several times.','断断续续的降雨数次推迟了户外仪式。'),ex(2,'The sensor sent intermittent signals whenever the battery weakened.','电池电量变弱时，传感器会间歇性地发出信号。')],mistakes:[m('The intermittent alarm rang without stopping for twelve hours.','The continuous alarm rang without stopping for twelve hours.','intermittent 表示时断时续；连续响十二小时应用 continuous。')],quiz:[q('intermittent',1,1,'Intermittent pain comes?','in episodes with periods of relief','continuously without any pause','only once and never again','intermittent 表示一阵阵发生，中间有停顿。'),q('intermittent',2,2,'An intermittent internet connection is?','sometimes available and sometimes lost','always fast and perfectly stable','permanently switched off','intermittent signal/service 会时有时无。'),q('intermittent',3,1,'Which description fits intermittent showers?','rain that starts and stops','rain that falls at a steady rate all day','a sky with no rain at all','阵雨常间歇发生，不会持续不停。'),q('intermittent',4,2,'The machine made intermittent noises overnight. The noises?','occurred with pauses between them','continued as one unbroken sound','were produced only in the morning','时断时续的声音之间存在停顿。')]});
D('internal',{etymology:{"origin":"Internal came through Medieval Latin internalis from Latin internus, within or inward; its deeper pre-Latin and PIE connections are reconstructed.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Internal came through Medieval Latin internalis from Latin internus, within or inward; its deeper pre-Latin and PIE connections are reconstructed."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective first described direction toward an interior and later anything situated inside a system or body.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深层的 PIE 形式属重建内容，这里不扩展未经核实的细节。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/internal"},contexts:[{"domain":"公司流程","senseId":"internal.s1","en":"The review found an internal error in the billing system, so the company corrected its own records before sending any revised invoices.","zh":"审查发现计费系统内部有一处错误，因此公司在寄出修订账单前先更正了自己的记录。","structure":"so 引出公司纠正措施，before 从句标明账单寄出前的时点。","grammar":"internal 修饰 error，表示错误发生在系统内部；its own 强调公司自身记录。","rationale":"internal 在此表示存在于某个系统里面，与客户外部信息无关。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'Doctors ordered a scan to check for internal bleeding.','医生安排扫描检查是否有内出血。'),ex(3,'The company resolved the dispute through an internal review.','公司通过内部审查解决了争议。'),ex(4,'He struggled with an internal conflict about whether to resign.','他内心挣扎，不知道是否应该辞职。')],mistakes:[m('The internal review was conducted by outside regulators with no company staff involved.','The external review was conducted by outside regulators with no company staff involved.','outside regulators 且无公司人员参与说明审查来自外部，应用 external 而非 internal。')],quiz:[q('internal',1,1,'An internal wall is located?','within a building or structure','along the outside boundary only','between two different countries','internal 指某物的里面或内部。'),q('internal',2,2,'Internal bleeding occurs?','inside the body','on the surface of a table','only in the national budget','医学中的 internal 可表示发生在身体内部。'),q('internal',3,3,'Internal trade takes place?','within one country','between two unrelated planets','only inside a single shop','internal affairs/trade 是一国内部事务或贸易。'),q('internal',4,4,'An internal conflict is a struggle?','within a person’s mind','between two foreign governments','between two rooms in a house','internal 也可形容内心发生的冲突。')]});
D('international',{etymology:{"origin":"International was coined by Jeremy Bentham in 1780 from inter-, between, and national, in his discussion of international jurisprudence.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"International was coined by Jeremy Bentham in 1780 from inter-, between, and national, in his discussion of international jurisprudence."}],"formationLogic":"The compound names matters situated between nations rather than within one country.","mnemonic":null,"note":"该词条明确将首用归于 Bentham。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/international"},contexts:[{"domain":"外交与贸易","senseId":"international.s1","en":"The international agreement requires each participating country to report emissions annually, although local agencies collect the measurements in different ways.","zh":"这项国际协议要求每个参与国每年报告排放量，尽管各地机构采用的测量方式不同。","structure":"although 从句承认测量方式不同，主句说明跨国共同义务。","grammar":"international 修饰 agreement；require + object + to-infinitive 表示正式要求。","rationale":"international 指涉及两个或更多国家，participating countries 和共同报告义务体现跨国关系。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The final attracted an international audience of millions.','这场决赛吸引了数百万国际观众。'),ex(3,'The young international scored twice for her country.','这位年轻的国手为国家队打入两球。')],mistakes:[m('The international trade agreement involved one country only and no foreign partners.','The domestic trade agreement involved one country only and no foreign partners.','international 通常涉及两个或更多国家；只有一国内部参与应称 domestic。')],quiz:[q('international',1,1,'An international conference includes participants from?','more than one country','one household only','one department in the same office','international 表示涉及多个国家。'),q('international',2,2,'A football international can mean?','a match between national teams','a local match between two school classes','a private training session','international 作名词可指国际赛事。'),q('international',3,3,'A swimming international is?','an athlete who represents their country','a swimming pool open all night','a visitor who cannot swim','international 可指代表国家参赛的运动员。'),q('international',4,1,'Which phrase is about relations among countries?','international diplomacy','interior decoration','personal interest','international diplomacy 涉及国家间关系。')]});
D('internationally',{etymology:{"origin":"Internationally is the adverb formed from international with -ly; international was coined in 1780 from inter- and national.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Internationally is the adverb formed from international with -ly; international was coined in 1780 from inter- and national."}],"formationLogic":"The adverb carries the adjective’s between-nations scope to describe how or where something is known.","mnemonic":null,"note":"依据国际词条所载 1821 年相关形式及常规 -ly 派生。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/international"},contexts:[{"domain":"文化交流","senseId":"internationally.s1","en":"The film became internationally known after subtitles made its dialogue accessible to viewers who did not speak the original language.","zh":"字幕让不会说原语言的观众也能理解对白后，这部电影在国际上广为人知。","structure":"after 从句交代传播条件，who 从句限定观众群体。","grammar":"internationally 修饰 known，说明知名度跨越多个国家。","rationale":"internationally 表示在许多国家或国际范围内，字幕带来的受众扩大与此对应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The research team is internationally recognized for its work on clean water.','这支研究团队因净水研究而享誉国际。')],mistakes:[m('The product is internationally sold in just one neighborhood and nowhere else.','The product is locally sold in just one neighborhood and nowhere else.','internationally 表示跨国或世界范围；仅在一个街区销售应为 locally。')],quiz:[q('internationally',1,1,'A musician known internationally is known?','in many countries','only by one neighbor','only inside one classroom','internationally 表示在国际范围内。'),q('internationally',2,1,'The charity works internationally. Where does it work?','across national borders','in one family’s home only','under the ocean only','internationally 修饰 work，说明活动遍及多个国家。'),q('internationally',3,1,'Which adjective does internationally come from?','international','interior','intermediate','internationally 是 international 加 -ly 构成的副词。'),q('internationally',4,1,'A company recognized internationally has?','a reputation in different countries','no customers outside its own room','a single local sign only','international recognition 指获得多国认可。')]});
D('Internet',{etymology:{"origin":"Internet arose from internetwork, a networking term recorded in 1974, and names the interconnected global computer network.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Internet arose from internetwork, a networking term recorded in 1974, and names the interconnected global computer network."}],"formationLogic":"The name combines inter- with network to describe networks linked together; the familiar shortened form became standard.","mnemonic":null,"note":"名称演变从 internetwork 到 Internet；网络基础设施与单个网站不可混同。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/Internet"},contexts:[{"domain":"数字通信","senseId":"Internet.s1","en":"The rural clinic uses the Internet to send test results securely to specialists in the city without asking patients to carry paper records.","zh":"乡村诊所利用互联网把检查结果安全地发送给城里的专科医生，无需患者携带纸质记录。","structure":"to send 表示使用网络的目的，without 短语说明避免的做法。","grammar":"the Internet 指全球互联网络；use A to do B 表示使用工具完成任务。","rationale":"此处 Internet 是连接计算机并传递信息的全球网络，而非泛指任一网站。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The library offers free access to the Internet for visitors.','图书馆向访客免费提供互联网接入。'),ex(2,'A stable Internet connection is needed for the remote lesson.','远程课程需要稳定的网络连接。')],mistakes:[m('I found the article at Internet while searching last night.','I found the article on the Internet while searching last night.','表示在互联网上查到信息，惯用 on the Internet，而不是 at Internet。')],quiz:[q('Internet',1,1,'The Internet is best described as?','a worldwide network connecting computer networks','one private computer in a classroom','a printed directory of telephone numbers','Internet 是连接全球计算机网络的系统。'),q('Internet',2,2,'If a hotel provides Internet access, guests can?','connect to online services','borrow the hotel’s television remote only','make calls without any network','Internet access 指连接互联网的服务。'),q('Internet',3,1,'Complete the usual phrase: She searched ___ the Internet.','on','at','into','常用搭配是 on the Internet。'),q('Internet',4,2,'The World Wide Web is?','a service available through the Internet','another name for every computer in the world','a physical cable under one street','万维网是互联网之上的信息服务，不等同于整个互联网。')]});
D('internist',{etymology:{"origin":"Internist is recorded from 1897, formed from internal medicine plus the agent or specialist suffix -ist.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Internist is recorded from 1897, formed from internal medicine plus the agent or specialist suffix -ist."}],"formationLogic":"The medical term names a doctor specializing in internal medicine rather than a hospital intern.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 将其词源直接分析为 internal medicine + -ist。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/internist"},contexts:[{"domain":"医疗就诊","senseId":"internist.s1","en":"The internist reviewed the patient’s blood tests and medication list before deciding whether the recurring fatigue required a specialist referral.","zh":"内科医生在判断反复疲劳是否需要转诊专科前，查看了患者的血液检测结果和用药清单。","structure":"before 从句说明作出转诊决定之前完成的检查，whether 从句是 deciding 的内容。","grammar":"internist 指内科医生；whether 引导间接疑问句。","rationale":"该医生评估内脏系统和一般成人疾病，符合 internist 的内科专科义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The internist reviewed her blood tests and referred her to a heart specialist.','内科医生查看了她的血液检查结果，并把她转诊给心脏专科医生。')],mistakes:[m('The internist repaired the apartment’s wiring and replaced the kitchen lights.','The electrician repaired the apartment’s wiring and replaced the kitchen lights.','internist 是内科医生，不负责修电路；此处职业应为 electrician。')],quiz:[q('internist',1,1,'An internist is a doctor who mainly treats?','medical problems involving internal organs','broken household appliances','injuries to buildings after a storm','internist 指以内科疾病为主要诊疗范围的医生。'),q('internist',2,1,'A patient with several non-surgical medical concerns may first see?','an internist','a building inspector','a music conductor','内科医生会诊治多种内科问题。'),q('internist',3,1,'The word internist is especially common in which variety of English?','American English','only medieval English','only Australian sign language','internist 是美式英语中常用的内科医生称呼。'),q('internist',4,1,'Which professional may coordinate care for an adult’s chronic illnesses?','an internist','a flight attendant','a tax accountant','成人慢性内科病可由 internist 评估和协调治疗。')]});
D('interpret',{etymology:{"origin":"Interpret came from Latin interpretari, to explain, translate, or expound, related to interpres, an interpreter or agent; the deeper origin of interpres is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interpret came from Latin interpretari, to explain, translate, or expound, related to interpres, an interpreter or agent; the deeper origin of interpres is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin verb’s translation sense passed into English and later broadened to explaining meaning and performing works.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁 interpres 的更深来源不确定，因此明确留白、不编造词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interpret"},contexts:[{"domain":"语言服务","senseId":"interpret.s1","en":"At the clinic, a trained interpreter interpreted the doctor’s instructions into Arabic while the patient asked questions in her first language.","zh":"在诊所里，受过训练的口译员把医生的指示口译成阿拉伯语，同时患者用自己的母语提问。","structure":"while 从句说明翻译进行时患者同时提问。","grammar":"interpret A into B 表示把 A 口译成 B；trained interpreter 是过去分词作定语。","rationale":"此处 interpret 指即时口译，而非对行为或文本作解释。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A volunteer interpreted the doctor’s instructions for the visiting family.','一名志愿者为来访家属口译了医生的指示。'),ex(3,'The jury interpreted his silence as uncertainty rather than agreement.','陪审团把他的沉默理解为犹豫，而不是同意。'),ex(4,'The pianist interpreted the final movement with unusual restraint.','钢琴家以不同寻常的克制演绎了最后一个乐章。')],mistakes:[m('She interpreted the printed novel into English over three months.','She translated the printed novel into English over three months.','interpret 的口译义指即时翻译口语；翻译书面小说通常用 translate。')],quiz:[q('interpret',1,1,'At a live meeting, an interpreter interprets when she?','translates speech as it is being spoken','prints a translated book months later','acts out a silent dance','interpret 可表示即时口译。'),q('interpret',2,2,'To interpret a graph is to?','explain what its information means','change the graph into a musical instrument','copy it without examining it','interpret data/graph 表示解释其含义。'),q('interpret',3,3,'I interpreted her nod as agreement. I?','understood the nod to mean she agreed','asked her to translate a speech','performed her role on stage','interpret X as Y 是把 X 理解为 Y。'),q('interpret',4,4,'A violinist interprets a concerto by?','performing it with a particular artistic understanding','explaining each word in another language','asking police questions about it','interpret a concerto 指演绎、演奏乐曲。')]});
D('interrogate',{etymology:{"origin":"Interrogate entered English as a late-fifteenth-century back-formation from interrogation or from Latin interrogatus, from interrogare, to ask or cross-examine, inter plus rogare, ask.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interrogate entered English as a late-fifteenth-century back-formation from interrogation or from Latin interrogatus, from interrogare, to ask or cross-examine, inter plus rogare, ask."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin components describe directing questions between or at someone during an inquiry.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深层 rogare 的 PIE 解释较复杂，此处止于拉丁语。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interrogate"},contexts:[{"domain":"刑事调查","senseId":"interrogate.s1","en":"Investigators interrogated the witness for two hours, but they stopped when she asked to contact a lawyer before answering further questions.","zh":"调查人员讯问了证人两个小时，但在她要求先联系律师再回答其他问题后停止了询问。","structure":"but 转折说明讯问暂停，when 从句给出暂停的时机。","grammar":"interrogate 表示长时间、仔细地提问；ask to contact 后接不定式。","rationale":"此处是警方讯问证人的义项，并非批判性地质询一个理论。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Investigators interrogated the witness separately for several hours.','调查人员分别讯问了这名证人好几个小时。'),ex(2,'The seminar encouraged students to interrogate the assumption that growth is always beneficial.','研讨课鼓励学生质疑增长总是有益这一假设。'),ex(3,'The analyst queried the database to interrogate records by date.','分析人员按日期查询数据库记录。')],mistakes:[m('The detective interrogated the suspect by asking no questions and ending the meeting immediately.','The detective questioned the suspect carefully before ending the meeting.','interrogate 意为仔细盘问，完全不提问且立即结束不符合这个动作。')],quiz:[q('interrogate',1,1,'Police interrogate a suspect when they?','question the suspect carefully about a case','offer the suspect a job without discussion','publish the suspect’s photograph as a portrait','警方 interrogate suspect 是审问、讯问嫌疑人。'),q('interrogate',2,2,'A critic interrogates an assumption by?','examining it with probing questions','accepting it without thought','hiding it from the discussion','学术语境的 interrogate 可指严肃质询、检验某个假设。'),q('interrogate',3,3,'A computer system is interrogated when a user?','queries it to retrieve information','turns off every database permanently','paints its outer casing','计算机语境中的 interrogate 指查询数据。'),q('interrogate',4,1,'Which activity most clearly counts as interrogation?','repeated, formal questioning about what happened','a brief greeting in a hallway','a written invitation to dinner','interrogation 是正式而细致的连续提问。')]});
D('interrupt',{etymology:{"origin":"Interrupt came from Latin interruptus, the past participle of interrumpere, to break off or break through, formed from inter and rumpere, break.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interrupt came from Latin interruptus, the past participle of interrumpere, to break off or break through, formed from inter and rumpere, break."}],"formationLogic":"The image of breaking into an ongoing act developed into stopping a speaker or process.","mnemonic":null,"note":"PIE 深层词根重建存在专门解释，这里只写可靠拉丁构词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interrupt"},contexts:[{"domain":"会议礼仪","senseId":"interrupt.s1","en":"Please let the speaker finish her explanation before you interrupt with a question, even if you think the answer is already clear.","zh":"即使你觉得答案已经很清楚，也请先让发言者讲完，再插话提问。","structure":"before 从句规定插话前要完成的动作，even if 表示让步条件。","grammar":"interrupt someone with something 表示以某事打断某人；let + object + verb。","rationale":"interrupt 指说话时打断他人，句中通过会议礼仪明确该义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'He interrupted the speaker to correct the date on the slide.','他打断发言者，指出幻灯片上的日期不对。'),ex(2,'A power failure interrupted the broadcast for several minutes.','停电使广播中断了几分钟。'),ex(4,'The sensor can detect a brief interruption in the current.','这个传感器可以检测到电流短暂中断。')],mistakes:[m('Please interrupt me after I have finished speaking, while I am still explaining the point.','Please interrupt me while I am speaking, if you need to ask something.','interrupt 是在对方说话或活动尚未完成时插入；等对方说完就不再是打断。')],quiz:[q('interrupt',1,1,'To interrupt a speaker is to?','stop them before they have finished speaking','listen until they have finished','summarize their speech afterward','interrupt sb 表示在对方说完前打断。'),q('interrupt',2,2,'A storm interrupted the match. What did it do?','stopped the match for a time','made the match more exciting','moved the match to another country','interrupt 也可指使活动暂时中断。'),q('interrupt',3,3,'A phone call interrupts someone’s work when it?','disturbs their work so they cannot continue smoothly','helps them finish without distraction','records the finished work','interrupt 也可指打扰某人正在做的事。'),q('interrupt',4,4,'The connection suffered an interruption. What occurred?','a temporary break in the connection','a permanent increase in speed','a new user account','名词 interruption 可指信号或过程的中断。')]});
D('intersect',{etymology:{"origin":"Intersect entered English in the seventeenth century, possibly as a back-formation from intersection or from Latin intersectus, from intersecare, to cut across, inter plus secare, cut.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intersect entered English in the seventeenth century, possibly as a back-formation from intersection or from Latin intersectus, from intersecare, to cut across, inter plus secare, cut."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin parts describe cutting across one another; the English verb later gained the common intransitive crossing sense.","mnemonic":null,"note":"早期词形来源有两个可能路径，故并列保留而不二选一。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intersect"},contexts:[{"domain":"地图与路线","senseId":"intersect.s1","en":"The two hiking trails intersect near a wooden bridge, where walkers can choose the shorter route back to the visitor center.","zh":"两条徒步路线在一座木桥附近相交，徒步者可以在那里选择较短路线返回游客中心。","structure":"where 从句说明相交处可进行的选择。","grammar":"the two trails 作复数主语，intersect 为不及物动词；where 回指 bridge 附近。","rationale":"intersect 表示两条线或路线交叉相遇，句中地点明确。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The two walking trails intersect beside the old water tower.','两条步道在旧水塔旁交汇。')],mistakes:[m('The two streets intersect, but they meet at no point and remain far apart.','The two streets run parallel, but they meet at no point and remain far apart.','intersect 表示相交；若路线始终不相遇，应说 run parallel。')],quiz:[q('intersect',1,1,'Two roads intersect when they?','cross or meet each other','run far apart without meeting','end at the same parking space','intersect 表示线、路或路径交叉。'),q('intersect',2,1,'If two circles intersect, they?','share one or more points','are both completely outside the page','have no possible relation','几何图形 intersect 时会有共同点。'),q('intersect',3,1,'Their research interests intersect. This means they?','overlap in some areas','never concern similar topics','belong to opposite centuries','兴趣或领域 intersect 可表示有重叠。'),q('intersect',4,1,'Choose the correct form: The two lines ___ at a right angle.','intersect','intersects','intersecting','复数主语 lines 应与动词原形 intersect 搭配。')]});
D('intersection',{etymology:{"origin":"Intersection came from Latin intersectionem, a cutting across, from intersecare, to cut asunder, with inter, between, and secare, cut.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intersection came from Latin intersectionem, a cutting across, from intersecare, to cut asunder, with inter, between, and secare, cut."}],"formationLogic":"The action noun first named crossing and later the place where streets or lines cross.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源先记几何交叉义，路口义为后来的空间用法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intersection"},contexts:[{"domain":"道路安全","senseId":"intersection.s1","en":"At the intersection, a delivery cyclist waited behind the white line until the traffic light changed and the pedestrian crossing cleared.","zh":"在十字路口，一名送货骑行者停在白线后，直到信号灯变换且人行横道畅通。","structure":"until 从句并列两个条件，说明骑行者等候的结束时机。","grammar":"at the intersection 定位路口；wait behind 与 until 引导的时间从句相连。","rationale":"intersection 指道路交会的地点，信号灯和人行横道场景对应道路义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A traffic light controls the intersection outside the school.','学校外的十字路口由交通信号灯控制。')],mistakes:[m('The two roads cross at the intersection, yet there is no point where they meet.','The two roads cross at the intersection, where they meet.','intersection 是道路相交处；否认它们在那里相遇与词义矛盾。')],quiz:[q('intersection',1,1,'Drivers slow down at an intersection because it is where?','roads meet or cross','cars are manufactured','a highway becomes a tunnel','intersection 指道路交叉处。'),q('intersection',2,1,'A four-way intersection usually connects?','four directions of road traffic','four separate train stations underground','one road with no exits','four-way intersection 是四个方向相接的路口。'),q('intersection',3,1,'Which word is closest in meaning for a road intersection?','junction','interval','intermission','junction 也可指道路交汇点。'),q('intersection',4,1,'A pedestrian should check both directions before crossing at an?','intersection','interview','intestine','行人需要在交叉路口确认车流后再过街。')]});
D('interval',{etymology:{"origin":"Interval came from Latin intervallum, originally the space between ramparts or stakes, from inter, between, and vallum, rampart.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interval came from Latin intervallum, originally the space between ramparts or stakes, from inter, between, and vallum, rampart."}],"formationLogic":"A spatial gap between defenses broadened to any measurable space or period between two things.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源的古罗马围栏解释对应早期空间义，现代时间义是扩展。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interval"},contexts:[{"domain":"医疗随访","senseId":"interval.s1","en":"The doctor scheduled the next scan at a six-month interval so that any change in the small growth could be detected early.","zh":"医生把下一次扫描安排在六个月后，以便尽早发现这个小增生是否发生变化。","structure":"so that 从句说明设置扫描间隔的目的。","grammar":"at a six-month interval 表示每隔六个月；could be detected 是被动语态。","rationale":"interval 在此是两次扫描之间的时间间隔，而非空间距离或幕间休息。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The medicine should be taken at six-hour intervals.','这种药应每隔六小时服用一次。'),ex(2,'Leave a short interval between each pair of seedlings.','每对幼苗之间留一小段距离。'),ex(3,'We bought drinks during the interval between the two acts.','两幕之间的休息时，我们买了饮料。'),ex(4,'The value 4 lies in the interval from 1 to 6.','数值 4 落在从 1 到 6 的区间内。')],mistakes:[m('The concert had no break between sections, but the audience went out during the interval.','The concert had a break between sections, and the audience went out during the interval.','观众在 interval 期间离场，说明演出有幕间休息；前半句说完全没有休息与之冲突。')],quiz:[q('interval',1,1,'Buses that run at ten-minute intervals arrive?','with ten minutes between scheduled buses','only ten minutes before sunrise','in groups of ten buses at once','时间义 interval 指两次事件之间的间隔。'),q('interval',2,2,'Planting trees at regular intervals means?','leaving consistent spaces between them','planting every tree in one hole','waiting until the trees become old','空间义 interval 是物体之间的距离。'),q('interval',3,3,'The audience returned after the interval. They returned after?','a short break during the performance','the final curtain had ended the whole show','a rehearsal at home','演出中的 interval 是幕间休息。'),q('interval',4,4,'In mathematics, an interval from 2 to 5 is?','a set or range of numbers between those values','a period when a theater is closed','the distance between two chairs only','数学中 interval 指两个端点之间的数值范围。')]});
D('intervene',{etymology:{"origin":"Intervene came from Latin intervenire, to come between, interrupt, or stand in the way, formed from inter, between, and venire, to come.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intervene came from Latin intervenire, to come between, interrupt, or stand in the way, formed from inter, between, and venire, to come."}],"formationLogic":"The compound literally places someone between parties, which developed into mediating or influencing events.","mnemonic":null,"note":"intervene 有经名词 intervention 回构的可能，但 Latin 来源也获支持，词源保持多源说法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intervene"},contexts:[{"domain":"冲突调解","senseId":"intervene.s2","en":"When the two colleagues began arguing over the schedule, their supervisor intervened and asked each person to explain the problem without interruption.","zh":"两位同事开始为日程争执时，主管介入并请双方分别不受打断地说明问题。","structure":"when 从句给出争执情形，and 连接主管介入后的两项做法。","grammar":"intervene 用不及物结构；ask + object + to-infinitive，without interruption 表示不受打断。","rationale":"这里 intervene 是为了改变局势而出面调停，符合调解义项。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The agency intervened to prevent the dispute from spreading.','该机构介入以防争端扩大。'),ex(2,'A mediator intervened between the families and helped them agree on a plan.','一名调解员在两家人之间进行调停，帮助他们达成计划。'),ex(3,'Several quiet years intervened before the two friends met again.','两位朋友再次见面之前，平静地过了好几年。')],mistakes:[m('The mediator intervened between the two sides by taking no action and refusing to speak to either side.','The mediator tried to remain neutral between the two sides by taking no action and refusing to speak to either side.','intervene 是主动介入以改变局势；完全不采取行动也不与双方沟通并非介入。')],quiz:[q('intervene',1,1,'A government intervenes in a dispute when it?','becomes involved to try to change the situation','watches but refuses to take any action','starts a different dispute elsewhere','intervene in 表示为了改变局势而介入。'),q('intervene',2,2,'A teacher intervenes between two arguing pupils to?','mediate and help settle their disagreement','make sure neither pupil can speak again','join the argument as a third opponent','intervene between people 可表示调停。'),q('intervene',3,3,'Years intervened before the team met again. This means?','several years passed between the meetings','the team met every day for years','the meetings happened at the same time','时间义 intervene 表示某段时间插在两件事之间。'),q('intervene',4,1,'Which construction is correct?','intervene in a conflict','intervene a conflict','intervene to a conflict','intervene 通常不及物，介入某事用 in。')]});
D('interview',{etymology:{"origin":"Interview combines inter- and view and was first used for a face-to-face meeting or consultation; the modern reporter-questioning sense developed later.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Interview combines inter- and view and was first used for a face-to-face meeting or consultation; the modern reporter-questioning sense developed later."}],"formationLogic":"The word’s historical parts suggest seeing one another; its present journalistic sense is a specialized question-and-answer meeting.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 对其构词和早期面谈义有记载；不将现代义倒推为词源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interview"},contexts:[{"domain":"新闻采访","senseId":"interview.s2","en":"The reporter interviewed the retired engineer about the bridge’s design, then checked every technical claim against the construction records.","zh":"记者就桥梁设计采访了退休工程师，然后将每项技术说法与施工记录逐一核对。","structure":"then 连接采访与事实核查的先后步骤。","grammar":"interview someone about something；check A against B 表示对照核实。","rationale":"interview 在此是记者向受访者提问的采访，而非求职面试。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She prepared examples of her work before the job interview.','求职面试前，她准备了几个工作案例。'),ex(2,'The reporter interviewed the mayor about the new transit plan.','记者就新的交通计划采访了市长。')],mistakes:[m('The reporter interviewed to the mayor for an hour about the new plan.','The reporter interviewed the mayor for an hour about the new plan.','interview 作动词可直接接被采访者作宾语，不说 interview to someone。')],quiz:[q('interview',1,1,'At a job interview, an employer asks questions to decide?','whether a candidate is suitable for the position','which news story should be published','how to repair the office printer','job interview 是评估求职者的面试。'),q('interview',2,2,'A newspaper interview with an author is usually?','a reporter’s question-and-answer meeting with the author','a test to determine the author’s blood type','a private job offer from the newspaper','传媒 interview 是记者或研究者的访谈。'),q('interview',3,3,'Which sentence uses interview as a verb correctly?','They interviewed four applicants.','They interviewed to four applicants.','They gave interview four applicants.','动词 interview 后直接接人作宾语。'),q('interview',4,1,'A candidate goes for an interview when they?','meet an employer who asks questions about the job','begin work without speaking to anyone','write a newspaper article about the firm','求职者参加面试是为了接受雇主提问。')]});
D('intestine',{etymology:{"origin":"Intestine came through Old French or directly from Latin intestinum, an inner part or entrail, from intestinus, internal, related to intus, within.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intestine came through Old French or directly from Latin intestinum, an inner part or entrail, from intestinus, internal, related to intus, within."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective for what lies inside became the name of an internal digestive organ.","mnemonic":null,"note":"远源拼写链有古法语或直接拉丁语两说，不强作唯一判断。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intestine"},contexts:[{"domain":"人体解剖","senseId":"intestine.s1","en":"The small intestine absorbs nutrients from digested food, while the large intestine removes water before the remaining waste leaves the body.","zh":"小肠从消化后的食物中吸收营养，而大肠在剩余废物排出体外前吸收水分。","structure":"while 对照小肠和大肠的功能，before 从句说明排出前的过程。","grammar":"small intestine 与 large intestine 构成固定解剖名称；while 连接对照事实。","rationale":"intestine 指胃以下的肠道器官，句中区分小肠和大肠的作用。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Food passes through the small intestine, where many nutrients are absorbed.','食物经过小肠，许多营养物质在这里被吸收。')],mistakes:[m('The intestine is a bone that protects the lungs inside the chest.','The rib cage is a bone structure that protects the lungs inside the chest.','intestine 是消化道的一部分，不是保护肺部的骨骼；这里应为 rib cage。')],quiz:[q('intestine',1,1,'The intestine is part of which body system?','the digestive system','the visual system','the skeletal system','intestine 指肠道，属于消化系统。'),q('intestine',2,1,'The small intestine mainly helps the body?','digest food and absorb nutrients','pump blood to the brain','control the movement of the eyes','小肠在消化和吸收营养中发挥作用。'),q('intestine',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','the small intestine','the small intestination','the small internal','small intestine 是常见器官名称。'),q('intestine',4,1,'A doctor examining the intestines is checking?','the digestive tract below the stomach','the bones in the hand','the outer layer of the skin','肠道位于胃以下，属于消化道。')]});
D('intimate',{etymology:{"origin":"Intimate as an adjective came through French intime from Latin intimus, innermost, the superlative form related to intus, within.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intimate as an adjective came through French intime from Latin intimus, innermost, the superlative form related to intus, within."}],"formationLogic":"The notion of being innermost extended from physical depth to close personal familiarity.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源说明用于形容词亲密义；intimate 作动词有另一路含义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intimate"},contexts:[{"domain":"友情与关系","senseId":"intimate.s1","en":"Although they had worked together for years, the two nurses became intimate friends only after caring for the same patients during a difficult winter.","zh":"尽管两位护士共事多年，她们是在艰难冬季共同照顾同一批患者后才成为亲密朋友。","structure":"although 让步从句先提共事时间，only after 强调友情形成的契机。","grammar":"intimate 修饰 friends，表示亲密关系；become 后接形容词加名词补语。","rationale":"intimate 在此指关系亲近，不表示隐私内容或精深知识。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The diary contains intimate details that she never shared publicly.','这本日记包含她从未公开分享过的私密细节。'),ex(3,'The guide has an intimate knowledge of the old harbor district.','这位向导对老港区了如指掌。'),ex(4,'The note intimated that the meeting might be postponed.','这张便条暗示会议可能会延期。'),ex(5,'Only his closest intimates knew why he had left the city.','只有他最亲近的密友知道他为什么离开这座城市。')],mistakes:[m('They are intimate friends, although they have never met, spoken, or communicated with each other.','They are strangers, since they have never met, spoken, or communicated with each other.','intimate friends 指关系非常亲近的人；彼此从未见面或交流与此直接冲突。')],quiz:[q('intimate',1,1,'Intimate friends usually have?','a very close personal relationship','no personal connection at all','only a professional contract','形容词 intimate 可表示私人关系亲密。'),q('intimate',2,2,'An intimate detail is?','private and personal','known publicly to everyone','a measurement of room size','intimate 也可指个人隐私或私密的细节。'),q('intimate',3,3,'He intimated that he might leave. He?','suggested it indirectly','announced it with a signed contract','denied it in a direct statement','动词 intimate 表示间接暗示。'),q('intimate',4,5,'A person’s intimates are their?','very close friends','medical examiners','distant competitors','名词 intimates 指亲密的朋友或密友。')]});
D('intimidate',{etymology:{"origin":"Intimidate came through French intimider from Latin timidus, fearful or timid, ultimately related to timere, to fear.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intimidate came through French intimider from Latin timidus, fearful or timid, ultimately related to timere, to fear."}],"formationLogic":"The verb developed causatively: to make another person feel timid or lose confidence.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁语 timidus 是可核对来源；更深 PIE 关系不在此补猜。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intimidate"},contexts:[{"domain":"公开演讲","senseId":"intimidate.s2","en":"The large audience initially intimidated the new presenter, but a supportive colleague helped her regain confidence before she began speaking.","zh":"庞大的观众起初让新演讲者感到胆怯，但一位支持她的同事在她开口前帮她恢复了信心。","structure":"but 转折呈现同事支持的效果，before 从句标出恢复信心的时点。","grammar":"intimidate + person；help + object + base verb 的结构是 help her regain。","rationale":"intimidate 在此表示使人丧失信心、望而生畏，而非直接以威胁强迫。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The witness said the gang tried to intimidate her into changing her account.','证人说那伙人试图恐吓她，让她改变陈述。'),ex(2,'The size of the first assignment intimidated the new student.','第一份作业的规模让新生望而生畏。')],mistakes:[m('The manager intimidated the witness by calmly assuring her that no one would threaten her.','The manager reassured the witness by calmly assuring her that no one would threaten her.','安抚并保证不会有人威胁她并非恐吓；此处应把 intimidate 改为 reassure。')],quiz:[q('intimidate',1,1,'A person tries to intimidate a witness in order to?','frighten or pressure the witness','help the witness feel safe','translate the witness’s statement','intimidate 可指故意恐吓、施压。'),q('intimidate',2,2,'A daunting first day may intimidate a new employee by?','making the employee lose confidence','giving the employee a formal promotion','making the employee an expert immediately','intimidate 也可指令某人望而生畏。'),q('intimidate',3,1,'Which phrase shows the intended pressure?','intimidate someone into silence','intimidate someone with a thank-you note','intimidate someone by reassuring them','intimidate sb into doing 表示威吓某人做某事。'),q('intimidate',4,2,'If a task intimidates you, you may feel?','nervous or lacking confidence about it','certain it will require no effort','unable to remember its name only','被任务吓住可能会感到紧张或缺乏信心。')]});
D('intimidating',{etymology:{"origin":"Intimidating is the present-participle adjective of intimidate, formed through French from Latin timidus, timid or fearful.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intimidating is the present-participle adjective of intimidate, formed through French from Latin timidus, timid or fearful."}],"formationLogic":"The -ing adjective describes the thing that causes the feeling of fear or loss of confidence.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此形容词直接源自动词 intimidate，不另设不确定词根。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intimidate"},contexts:[{"domain":"学习与挑战","senseId":"intimidating.s1","en":"The unfamiliar control panel looked intimidating at first, yet the technician learned each function by following the numbered steps in the manual.","zh":"陌生的控制面板起初看起来很吓人，但技术员按照手册中的编号步骤逐一学会了各项功能。","structure":"yet 转折呈现从畏惧到掌握的变化，by following 说明学习方式。","grammar":"look + adjective；intimidating 描述使人感到畏惧的事物。","rationale":"intimidating 表示让人害怕或失去信心，陌生复杂的面板构成具体来源。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The intimidating entrance exam seemed difficult, but the instructions were clear.','这场令人望而生畏的入学考试看起来很难，但说明写得很清楚。')],mistakes:[m('The intimidating speech made everyone feel completely relaxed and unafraid.','The reassuring speech made everyone feel completely relaxed and unafraid.','intimidating 表示令人害怕或胆怯；让人安心的演讲应称 reassuring。')],quiz:[q('intimidating',1,1,'An intimidating building may make visitors feel?','nervous or overawed','hungry for dinner','certain they are at home','intimidating 描述使人胆怯的事物。'),q('intimidating',2,1,'An intimidating opponent is one who seems?','likely to make others feel afraid or less confident','unable to affect anyone’s confidence','interested only in interior design','intimidating 常形容令人畏惧的对手。'),q('intimidating',3,1,'Which noun naturally follows intimidating?','prospect','intimidatingly person','intimidatingnessly','intimidating 可自然修饰 prospect，表示令人望而生畏的前景。'),q('intimidating',4,1,'A difficult task can seem intimidating even if it is?','manageable once someone begins','already finished before it starts','unrelated to the person doing it','令人生畏描述感受，不等于任务绝对无法完成。')]});
D('into',{etymology:{"origin":"Into is an Old English compound of in and to, expressing movement from outside toward a position inside.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Into is an Old English compound of in and to, expressing movement from outside toward a position inside."}],"formationLogic":"The older preposition combines location in with the directional force of to.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词条其余转换、碰撞、除法和兴趣义不在本语境中。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/into"},contexts:[{"domain":"搬家与收纳","senseId":"into.s1","en":"The movers carried the boxes into the new apartment one at a time, checking each label so fragile dishes would not be placed under heavy books.","zh":"搬运工一次把一个箱子搬进新公寓，并检查每个标签，以免易碎餐具被压在沉重的书下面。","structure":"one at a time 表示逐个搬运，so 引出检查标签的目的。","grammar":"carry something into a place 表示向内移动；would not be placed 是目的从句中的被动形式。","rationale":"into 表示从外部移动到某个空间内部，箱子进入公寓是明确的方向义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The child stepped into the shallow pool with an adult beside him.','孩子在一位成人陪伴下走进浅水池。'),ex(2,'The caterpillar turned into a butterfly over several weeks.','几周内，毛毛虫变成了一只蝴蝶。'),ex(3,'The cyclist crashed into a barrier at the corner.','骑车人在拐角处撞上了护栏。'),ex(4,'In long division, 4 goes into 20 five times.','在长除法中，4 除 20 得 5。'),ex(5,'She is really into jazz and goes to concerts every month.','她很喜欢爵士乐，每个月都去听音乐会。')],mistakes:[m('The package is into the box already, resting inside it on the shelf.','The package is in the box already, resting inside it on the shelf.','静态地表示已经在里面用 in；into 通常强调进入的移动过程。')],quiz:[q('into',1,1,'The cat ran into the room. Which idea does into express?','movement from outside to inside','a fixed location with no movement','movement away from the room','into 表示向某物内部移动。'),q('into',2,2,'The snow turned into water. What happened?','It changed into a different state.','It entered a room without moving.','It was divided by a number.','turn into 表示转变成另一种状态。'),q('into',3,3,'The car ran into a fence. It?','hit the fence accidentally','drove away from every fence','became a fence','run into 可表示意外撞上。'),q('into',4,5,'If a student is into robotics, the student?','is very interested in robotics','has been physically placed inside a robot','refuses to learn about robotics','口语 be into 表示对某活动或领域很感兴趣。')]});
D('intolerant',{etymology:{"origin":"Intolerant combines the negative prefix in- with tolerant, from tolerate, ultimately from Latin tolerare, to bear or endure.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intolerant combines the negative prefix in- with tolerant, from tolerate, ultimately from Latin tolerare, to bear or endure."}],"formationLogic":"The prefix reverses tolerance, yielding the sense of refusing to accept differing opinions or conditions.","mnemonic":null,"note":"派生构词透明；拉丁 tolerare 的远源不进一步推定。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intolerant"},contexts:[{"domain":"公共讨论","senseId":"intolerant.s1","en":"A tolerant moderator lets people disagree respectfully, whereas an intolerant moderator dismisses every view that differs from her own.","zh":"宽容的主持人允许人们尊重地表达不同意见，而不宽容的主持人会否定所有与自己不同的观点。","structure":"whereas 对比两种主持风格，that 从句修饰 view。","grammar":"intolerant 由否定前缀 in- 加 tolerant 构成；differ from 表示与……不同。","rationale":"intolerant 表示不接纳他人观点，后半句具体说明了这种态度。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The policy is intolerant of religious differences and excludes several groups.','这项政策不容忍宗教差异，并排斥了几个群体。')],mistakes:[m('She is intolerant of other opinions and welcomes every viewpoint equally.','She is tolerant of other opinions and welcomes every viewpoint equally.','欢迎不同观点与 intolerant of 矛盾；这里应改为 tolerant。')],quiz:[q('intolerant',1,1,'An intolerant attitude toward disagreement is?','unwilling to accept other views','eager to consider different opinions','unrelated to anyone’s beliefs','intolerant 描述不接受、不能容忍异见。'),q('intolerant',2,1,'A person intolerant of criticism is likely to?','react badly when criticized','ask for more feedback','welcome every negative comment','intolerant of criticism 表示不能接受批评。'),q('intolerant',3,1,'Which preposition follows intolerant in this use?','of','at','between','常用结构是 intolerant of something。'),q('intolerant',4,1,'Which behavior is most clearly intolerant?','refusing to let others express a different belief','listening respectfully to a disagreement','changing one’s mind after considering evidence','不允许他人表达异见体现不宽容。')]});
D('intoxicated',{etymology:{"origin":"Intoxicated is the past-participle form of intoxicate, from Medieval Latin intoxicare, to poison, built from Latin toxicum, poison, via Greek toxikon.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intoxicated is the past-participle form of intoxicate, from Medieval Latin intoxicare, to poison, built from Latin toxicum, poison, via Greek toxikon."}],"formationLogic":"The word first carried a poisoning sense and broadened to impairment from alcohol or drugs.","mnemonic":null,"note":"保留由中世纪拉丁语及希腊语毒物词汇传入的路径，不拆解为 in- + toxic。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intoxicate"},contexts:[{"domain":"公共安全","senseId":"intoxicated.s1","en":"The driver was visibly intoxicated after the party, so a friend took the car keys and arranged a taxi instead.","zh":"聚会后，这名司机明显喝醉了，因此朋友拿走车钥匙，改为安排出租车。","structure":"so 引出安全应对措施，instead 表示以出租车替代自行驾车。","grammar":"be intoxicated 表示处于醉酒状态；arrange a taxi 是合理替代方案。","rationale":"intoxicated 在此指酒精导致的醉态，并由拿走车钥匙这一行动体现风险。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The driver was intoxicated, so the police arranged a safe ride home.','司机喝醉了，因此警方安排了安全送返。')],mistakes:[m('The driver was intoxicated, but had consumed no alcohol or other impairing substance and showed no signs of impairment.','The driver was sober and showed no signs of impairment.','intoxicated 指受酒精影响而醉；没有摄入相关物质且无受影响迹象时应说 sober。')],quiz:[q('intoxicated',1,1,'An intoxicated person has usually been affected by?','alcohol','a short walk outdoors','a cup of plain water','intoxicated 在该来源义中指饮酒后醉的状态。'),q('intoxicated',2,1,'A sign warning against driving while intoxicated warns people not to drive when?','their judgment and control are impaired by alcohol','they have just washed the car','they are carrying a paper map','酒后判断和控制能力受影响，不应驾驶。'),q('intoxicated',3,1,'Which word is closest in everyday meaning?','drunk','hungry','asleep','intoxicated 与 drunk 意思接近，但语体更正式。'),q('intoxicated',4,1,'A person who is intoxicated should?','avoid driving and arrange a safe way home','operate heavy machinery alone','decide that impairment is impossible','饮酒后受影响的人应避免驾驶并确保安全返家。')]});
D('intractable',{etymology:{"origin":"Intractable came through Latin intractabilis, not manageable or not to be handled, from in- plus tractare, to handle or manage, with -able.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intractable came through Latin intractabilis, not manageable or not to be handled, from in- plus tractare, to handle or manage, with -able."}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix turns tractable, capable of being handled, into something resistant to solution.","mnemonic":null,"note":"tractare 的更深来源不展开；此处只用拉丁派生链。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intractable"},contexts:[{"domain":"公共政策","senseId":"intractable.s1","en":"The intractable housing shortage persisted because construction costs rose faster than wages and several proposed sites lacked reliable transport links.","zh":"住房短缺问题棘手且持续存在，因为建筑成本上涨快于工资，而且几个拟议地块缺少可靠交通连接。","structure":"because 从句列出问题难以解决的两个原因。","grammar":"intractable 修饰 housing shortage；because 内有并列谓语 persisted 与 lacked。","rationale":"intractable 表示难以控制或解决，成本和交通障碍具体说明其棘手。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The team needed several years to find a workable response to the intractable water shortage.','团队花了好几年才找到应对这一棘手缺水问题的可行办法。')],mistakes:[m('The intractable puzzle was solved immediately with one obvious move.','The simple puzzle was solved immediately with one obvious move.','intractable 强调难以解决或控制；一步就能显然解决的谜题并不棘手。')],quiz:[q('intractable',1,1,'An intractable problem is difficult to?','solve or manage','notice because it is brightly colored','describe in one short sentence','intractable 指难以解决或控制。'),q('intractable',2,1,'An intractable conflict may require?','a long and difficult effort to resolve','one routine form with no discussion','no action because it ended already','棘手冲突通常需要持续努力才能解决。'),q('intractable',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','an intractable disease','an intractable breakfast plate','intractably person','intractable 可形容难治或难控制的疾病。'),q('intractable',4,1,'If negotiations remain intractable, the disagreement is?','still hard to settle','already settled easily','not connected to any issue','remain intractable 表示仍然难以解决。')]});
D('intricate',{etymology:{"origin":"Intricate came from Latin intricatus, entangled, the past participle of intricare, to entangle, related to tricae, perplexities or hindrances.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intricate came from Latin intricatus, entangled, the past participle of intricare, to entangle, related to tricae, perplexities or hindrances."}],"formationLogic":"A word for entangling developed the sense of something complicated through many interrelated parts.","mnemonic":null,"note":"tricae 的更深语源有不确定因素，此处止于可查的拉丁词形。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intricate"},contexts:[{"domain":"工程设计","senseId":"intricate.s1","en":"The engineer mapped how each cable crossed the others before removing the old wiring, because the intricate network connected sensors in several rooms.","zh":"拆除旧线路前，工程师绘出了每根电缆交叉的位置，因为这套错综复杂的网络连接着几个房间的传感器。","structure":"before 从句说明拆线前的准备，because 从句解释绘图必要性。","grammar":"how 引导 mapped 的宾语从句；intricate 修饰 network。","rationale":"intricate 表示多个相互关联部分构成复杂整体，电缆连接传感器体现这种结构。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The watchmaker opened the intricate mechanism with a pair of fine tools.','钟表匠用一把精细工具打开了这套复杂的机械装置。'),ex(2,'The silver bowl bears intricate patterns carved by hand.','这只银碗上刻着手工雕成的精细图案。')],mistakes:[m('The intricate design contains only one plain line and no small details.','The simple design contains only one plain line and no small details.','intricate 强调结构复杂或细节繁多；只有一条简单线条不符合这个意思。')],quiz:[q('intricate',1,1,'An intricate mechanism has?','many connected parts arranged in a complex way','no moving parts or details','only one large and simple piece','intricate 常指由多部分构成、关系复杂。'),q('intricate',2,2,'An intricate carving is likely to show?','many fine details','a blank and smooth surface','a single rough cut only','intricate 也可形容工艺细节精巧繁复。'),q('intricate',3,1,'Which phrase is a natural collocation?','an intricate plot','an intricately plot','an intricateness plot','intricate plot 是形容情节复杂的自然搭配。'),q('intricate',4,2,'The lace has intricate stitching. The stitching is?','carefully detailed and elaborate','missing from the whole piece','made from a single unworked thread','intricate stitching 表示精细繁复的针脚。')]});
D('intrigue',{etymology:{"origin":"Intrigue came through French intriguer and Italian intrigare from Latin intricare, to entangle; the English noun first referred to a complicated secret plot.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intrigue came through French intriguer and Italian intrigare from Latin intricare, to entangle; the English noun first referred to a complicated secret plot."}],"formationLogic":"The idea of entanglement developed into plots and then figuratively into something that captures curiosity.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处取动词的好奇义；词源中 plot 义先于现代引起兴趣的用法。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intrigue"},contexts:[{"domain":"悬疑故事","senseId":"intrigue.s2","en":"The missing page intrigued the archivist because the remaining letters hinted that the author had changed the ending shortly before publication.","zh":"缺失的那一页引起了档案管理员的强烈好奇，因为残存信件暗示作者在出版前不久改动过结尾。","structure":"because 从句解释好奇的理由，that 从句作 hinted 的内容。","grammar":"intrigue 在此作及物动词；intrigue someone 表示使某人感到好奇。","rationale":"intrigue 选择使人非常感兴趣的动词义，不是秘密阴谋的名词义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The film reveals a court intrigue involving a forged royal letter.','影片揭示了一场涉及伪造王室信件的宫廷阴谋。'),ex(2,'The unexplained mark on the map intrigued the researchers.','地图上那个无法解释的标记引起了研究人员的好奇。'),ex(3,'The officials intrigued against the governor in secret.','这些官员暗中密谋反对州长。')],mistakes:[m('The unexplained map intrigued the researchers, so they felt no curiosity and ignored it completely.','The unexplained map intrigued the researchers, so they became curious and examined it.','intrigue 作动词表示引起好奇；毫无好奇且完全忽略与后半句的结果矛盾。')],quiz:[q('intrigue',1,1,'A political intrigue is a?','secret plan, often involving harmful or illegal action','public schedule for a town meeting','simple explanation of a weather report','intrigue 作名词可指秘密阴谋。'),q('intrigue',2,2,'A strange clue intrigues a detective when it?','makes the detective curious to learn more','proves there is nothing to investigate','orders the detective to stop working','intrigue 作动词表示引发强烈兴趣。'),q('intrigue',3,3,'Officials who intrigue against a leader are?','secretly plotting against the leader','publicly supporting every decision','studying the leader’s handwriting openly','intrigue against 表示暗中密谋反对。'),q('intrigue',4,2,'Which reaction best matches being intrigued?','wanting to discover the answer','feeling certain there is nothing unusual','forgetting the subject immediately','被某事 intrigue 通常会感到好奇、想继续了解。')]});
D('intrinsic',{etymology:{"origin":"Intrinsic came through Medieval Latin intrinsecus, inwardly or on the inside, and French intrinseque; the exact internal formation is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intrinsic came through Medieval Latin intrinsecus, inwardly or on the inside, and French intrinseque; the exact internal formation is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The historical inward sense developed into the modern meaning belonging naturally to something itself.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不把 intrinsecus 强行拆成英语词素，其内部来源未确立。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intrinsic"},contexts:[{"domain":"科学与材料","senseId":"intrinsic.s1","en":"A material’s intrinsic strength remains even when its surface is scratched, although the damaged coating may make the object less durable in practice.","zh":"即使表面被划伤，材料本身的强度仍然存在，尽管受损涂层在实际使用中可能降低物体的耐用性。","structure":"although 从句区分材料固有属性与外部涂层造成的实际影响。","grammar":"intrinsic 修饰 strength，表示属性来自材料自身；although 引导让步。","rationale":"intrinsic 指本身自然具有、非外界赋予的特性，与外部 coating 构成对照。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The award recognizes the intrinsic value of careful, honest research.','这个奖项认可严谨、诚实的研究本身所具有的价值。'),ex(2,'The intrinsic muscles of the hand help control small finger movements.','手部内在肌有助于控制手指的细微动作。')],mistakes:[m('The intrinsic value of the medal comes only from its current market price, not from anything inherent in it.','The extrinsic value of the medal comes only from its current market price, not from anything inherent in it.','intrinsic 指事物自身固有的价值；仅由外部市场价格决定的是 extrinsic。')],quiz:[q('intrinsic',1,1,'An intrinsic quality belongs to something?','as part of its own nature','only because an outside person assigns it','only for one temporary day','intrinsic 表示内在固有，而非外部赋予。'),q('intrinsic',2,1,'The intrinsic value of a friendship is value that?','comes from the relationship itself','depends only on its resale price','is measured by its location','intrinsic value 是事物本身具有的价值。'),q('intrinsic',3,2,'Intrinsic muscles of the hand are located?','within the hand itself','outside the body in a glove','inside the stomach','医学解剖义 intrinsic 指位于身体或器官内部。'),q('intrinsic',4,1,'Which preposition fits: The risk is intrinsic ___ the activity.','to','at','from','intrinsic 常与 to 连用，表示某性质内在于某事物。')]});
D('introduce',{etymology:{"origin":"Introduce came from Latin introductus, the past participle of introducere, to lead in, formed from intro, inward, and ducere, to lead.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Introduce came from Latin introductus, the past participle of introducere, to lead in, formed from intro, inward, and ducere, to lead."}],"formationLogic":"The literal notion of leading someone in developed into presenting one person to another.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁构词来源清楚，此处只选介绍人的义项。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/introduce"},contexts:[{"domain":"初次见面","senseId":"introduce.s1","en":"At the workshop, the host introduced the visiting scientist to the local teachers before inviting everyone to share one research question.","zh":"研讨会上，主持人在邀请大家分享一个研究问题前，先把来访科学家介绍给当地教师。","structure":"before 短语标出介绍和讨论活动的顺序。","grammar":"introduce A to B 表示把 A 介绍给 B；before inviting 中 inviting 用动名词。","rationale":"introduce 在这里是让双方知道彼此姓名并相识，不是引进产品或提出话题。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The host introduced the two visiting researchers before dinner.','晚餐前，主人把两位来访研究员介绍给彼此。'),ex(2,'The city introduced a new permit system for shared bicycles.','市里为共享单车推出了新的许可制度。'),ex(3,'The lecturer introduced the topic with a short historical example.','讲师用一个简短的历史案例引出了这个话题。'),ex(4,'Her uncle introduced her to classical music when she was a child.','她小时候，叔叔让她初次接触了古典音乐。')],mistakes:[m('She introduced me the new manager at the reception.','She introduced me to the new manager at the reception.','introduce A to B 的结构中，表示引见给某人时需要介词 to。')],quiz:[q('introduce',1,1,'To introduce two guests is to?','tell them each other’s names so they can meet','ask them to leave before they arrive','publish their private letters','introduce people 可指引见、介绍。'),q('introduce',2,2,'A government introduces a new law when it?','brings the law into use','removes it from every record','translates it but never adopts it','introduce a law 表示提出并推行新法律。'),q('introduce',3,3,'A speaker introduces a topic by?','opening the discussion with it','ending the discussion before it starts','changing the topic without mention','introduce a topic 是引出讨论主题。'),q('introduce',4,4,'A mentor introduces a student to research by?','helping the student experience it for the first time','introducing the student’s name to a crowd','banning the student from reading','introduce someone to something 可指使其初次接触。')]});
D('introduction',{etymology:{"origin":"Introduction came from Late Latin introductionem, an act of leading in, from introductus, the past participle of Latin introducere, to lead in.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Introduction came from Late Latin introductionem, an act of leading in, from introductus, the past participle of Latin introducere, to lead in."}],"formationLogic":"The noun names the act of bringing something in and its resulting opening or introductory section.","mnemonic":null,"note":"不将英语前缀 in- 单独分析；历史构词是拉丁 intro- + ducere。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/introduction"},contexts:[{"domain":"学术写作","senseId":"introduction.s1","en":"The introduction explains why the survey matters, defines the key terms, and previews the sections that present the results.","zh":"引言说明这项调查为何重要，界定关键术语，并概述展示结果的各个部分。","structure":"三个并列谓语说明引言的组成任务。","grammar":"introduction 作名词指引入或介绍；that 从句修饰 sections。","rationale":"此处 introduction 是文章开头的介绍部分，通过功能说明对应词条义项。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The introduction explains why the study focuses on rural schools.','引言解释了这项研究为何聚焦乡村学校。')],mistakes:[m('The book’s introduction appears after the final chapter and contains the closing summary.','The book’s conclusion appears after the final chapter and contains the closing summary.','introduction 通常在开篇介绍内容；书末总结应称 conclusion。')],quiz:[q('introduction',1,1,'A book’s introduction usually?','presents the subject before the main chapters','lists every result after the final chapter','replaces the index of names','introduction 常指书或文章开头的介绍。'),q('introduction',2,1,'At a reception, an introduction helps two people?','meet and learn each other’s names','avoid speaking to each other','exchange their legal identities','introduction 也指把人引见认识。'),q('introduction',3,1,'A short introduction to a topic gives readers?','basic information before the details','only the final answer with no context','a complete list of unrelated topics','introduction 可提供主题背景和开端。'),q('introduction',4,1,'Which part commonly comes near the beginning of a report?','the introduction','the afterword only','the final appendix only','报告通常先有 introduction，再展开正文。')]});
D('intrude',{etymology:{"origin":"Intrude entered English from Latin intrudere, to thrust or force in, formed from in-, in, and trudere, to push; its social sense developed from physical entry.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intrude entered English from Latin intrudere, to thrust or force in, formed from in-, in, and trudere, to push; its social sense developed from physical entry."}],"formationLogic":"The literal pushing-in image shifted to entering a private place or conversation without invitation.","mnemonic":null,"note":"早期 ecclesiastical 用法及后来的日常语义变化按词源词典记录。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intrude"},contexts:[{"domain":"隐私与社交","senseId":"intrude.s1","en":"I did not want to intrude on their family dinner, so I sent a message asking whether they were free to talk later.","zh":"我不想打扰他们的家庭晚餐，于是发消息询问他们晚些时候是否有空交谈。","structure":"so 连接避免打扰和改用消息的做法，whether 从句作 asking 的内容。","grammar":"intrude on someone’s time or privacy 表示未经欢迎地打扰；later 修饰 talk。","rationale":"intrude 在此表示不请自来地进入他人的私人时间，而非物理闯入场所。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A reporter intruded into the private garden despite the closed gate.','尽管大门关着，一名记者还是闯进了私人花园。'),ex(2,'I am sorry to intrude while you are having dinner.','你们吃饭时打扰了，抱歉。'),ex(3,'The lawyer warned the witness not to intrude personal opinions into the factual report.','律师提醒证人不要把个人意见强加到事实报告中。')],mistakes:[m('The photographer intruded on their privacy by never entering their private space or disturbing them.','The photographer respected their privacy by staying away and not disturbing them.','从未进入私人空间或打扰对方不能称为 intrude on their privacy。')],quiz:[q('intrude',1,1,'Someone intrudes into a locked room when they?','enter without permission','wait to be invited inside','repair its lock from outside','intrude into 表示不受欢迎或未经许可地闯入。'),q('intrude',2,2,'“Sorry to intrude” is said when someone?','may be disturbing another person’s private time','has been invited to give a formal speech','is asking for directions in a public station','intrude 也可表示打扰他人的私人时间。'),q('intrude',3,3,'To intrude your opinions on others is to?','force your views into a situation','listen carefully without commenting','withdraw your views from the discussion','intrude something on/upon someone 指把想法强加给别人。'),q('intrude',4,1,'Which preposition fits: He intruded ___ their conversation.','into','at','from','表示闯入谈话常用 intrude into。')]});
D('intuition',{etymology:{"origin":"Intuition came from Late Latin intuitionem, a looking at or consideration, from Latin intueri, to look at or consider, with in- and tueri.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Intuition came from Late Latin intuitionem, a looking at or consideration, from Latin intueri, to look at or consider, with in- and tueri."}],"formationLogic":"A noun for looking or considering developed into immediate cognition without conscious reasoning.","mnemonic":null,"note":"tueri 的更深词源被认为不确定，故不扩展超出拉丁语。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intuition"},contexts:[{"domain":"判断与经验","senseId":"intuition.s1","en":"Her intuition told her that the cheerful email was incomplete, so she called the supplier and confirmed that the delivery date had changed.","zh":"她的直觉告诉她，这封语气愉快的邮件并不完整，因此她致电供应商确认了交货日期已经变更。","structure":"so 引出核实行动，that 从句补充直觉判断和确认内容。","grammar":"intuition 作主语；tell someone that 引导所知内容。","rationale":"intuition 指无需逐步推理便能察觉某事的能力，随后打电话是将直觉核实。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her intuition told her that the quiet witness was hiding an important detail.','她的直觉告诉她，那位沉默的证人隐瞒了一个重要细节。'),ex(2,'I had an intuition that the road would be closed after the storm.','我有种直觉，暴风雨后这条路会封闭。')],mistakes:[m('He reached the conclusion by intuition alone after listing every premise and proving each step logically.','He reached the conclusion by logical deduction after listing every premise and proving each step.','逐项列出前提并证明每一步，说明结论来自逻辑推演，而不是 intuition alone。')],quiz:[q('intuition',1,1,'A person who acts on intuition often relies on?','an immediate sense without working through every step','a complete written proof for every choice','a measurement that removes all judgment','intuition 指不经逐步推理形成的直觉判断。'),q('intuition',2,2,'She had an intuition that the plan would fail. This was?','a feeling that it would fail without clear proof','a signed report proving it had failed','a detailed measurement of its cost','intuition 也可指某种未经证明的直觉感受。'),q('intuition',3,1,'A doctor’s clinical intuition may help them?','notice a pattern quickly from experience','avoid examining a patient altogether','replace every medical test by guessing','intuition 是迅速理解的能力，仍不能代替必要检查。'),q('intuition',4,2,'Which phrase is natural?','I had an intuition that something was wrong.','I had an intuition to something was wrong.','I had an intuitive that something was wrong.','intuition 可接 that 从句说明直觉内容。')]});
D('inundate',{etymology:{"origin":"Inundate appeared in English in the seventeenth century, as a back-formation from inundation or from Latin inundatus, past participle of inundare, to overflow.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Inundate appeared in English in the seventeenth century, as a back-formation from inundation or from Latin inundatus, past participle of inundare, to overflow."}],"formationLogic":"The verb retains the literal Latin sense of water flowing over land.","mnemonic":null,"note":"其更深水词根由 inundation 页面记载；当前只依赖可核对的拉丁来源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inundate"},contexts:[{"domain":"灾害应对","senseId":"inundate.s1","en":"The storm could inundate the lower fields before dawn, so farmers moved the animals to higher ground when the river began to rise.","zh":"暴风雨可能在黎明前淹没低地田野，因此河水开始上涨时，农民把牲畜转移到高处。","structure":"so 表示预警后的措施，when 从句指出转移动作的触发信号。","grammar":"inundate 后接被淹没的地点；could 表示可能性。","rationale":"此处 inundate 是洪水淹没土地的字面义，不是信息或工作大量涌来。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Seasonal floods inundate the low fields beside the river.','季节性洪水淹没了河边的低洼田地。')],mistakes:[m('The levee held back the river and inundated every nearby field with floodwater.','The levee failed to hold back the river, which inundated every nearby field with floodwater.','堤坝挡住洪水与洪水淹没附近田地的结果矛盾；说明堤坝失效即可。')],quiz:[q('inundate',1,1,'Floodwater inundates a village when it?','covers or floods the village','dries every road in it','builds a wall around it','inundate 的本义是淹没、使泛滥。'),q('inundate',2,1,'Fields inundated after heavy rain are?','covered by water','burned by sunlight','cleared of all crops','洪水可 inundate 低洼田地。'),q('inundate',3,1,'Which object can naturally follow inundate in the source sense?','the farmland','a spoken sentence only','a musical rhythm','inundate 可直接接被水淹没的地点或土地。'),q('inundate',4,1,'Choose the correct past form: The river ___ the plain last spring.','inundated','inundateed','inundating','inundate 的过去式直接加 -d，拼作 inundated。')]});
D('inundation',{etymology:{"origin":"Inundation came from Latin inundationem, a noun for overflowing, from inundare, to overflow, formed with in- and undare, to flow, from unda, wave.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Inundation came from Latin inundationem, a noun for overflowing, from inundare, to overflow, formed with in- and undare, to flow, from unda, wave."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin noun names the event or result of water flowing over a boundary.","mnemonic":null,"note":"更深的 PIE 水词根是重建形式；词源说明保留在可核实拉丁和词族范围。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inundation"},contexts:[{"domain":"洪水与地形","senseId":"inundation.s1","en":"After the inundation, volunteers marked the highest waterline on each building so engineers could map the areas most exposed to future floods.","zh":"洪水退去后，志愿者在每栋建筑上标出最高水位线，以便工程师绘制未来最容易遭受洪水的区域。","structure":"after 从句确定时间背景，so 引出标记水线的用途。","grammar":"inundation 作名词指洪水；so engineers could map 表示目的或预期结果。","rationale":"inundation 是大范围水流溢出形成的洪水，留下水位线用于灾后测绘。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'After the inundation, mud and branches covered the village road.','洪水泛滥后，泥土和树枝覆盖了村道。')],mistakes:[m('The inundation left every field completely dry and untouched by water.','The drought left every field completely dry and untouched by water.','inundation 指水灾或泛滥，田地干燥且未沾水更符合 drought。')],quiz:[q('inundation',1,1,'An inundation is a large amount of?','floodwater covering an area','dry dust in an empty room','fresh air entering a building','inundation 是洪水泛滥或水淹。'),q('inundation',2,1,'A report on an inundation would likely describe?','flood damage to homes and fields','a routine harvest with no rain','a new bridge opening ceremony','洪灾报告常记录水淹造成的损失。'),q('inundation',3,1,'Which event could cause an inundation?','a river overflowing its banks','a week without any water','a road being repainted','河水漫出河岸会导致淹水。'),q('inundation',4,1,'Which verb is closest in meaning to inundation’s root action?','flood','freeze','irrigate','inundation 与 flood 同属洪水泛滥的意思。')]});
D('invade',{etymology:{"origin":"Invade came from Latin invadere, to go into, fall upon, or attack, formed from in-, into, and vadere, to go or advance.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invade came from Latin invadere, to go into, fall upon, or attack, formed from in-, into, and vadere, to go or advance."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin motion verb developed into the hostile sense of entering a territory by force.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此处选择军事义，不把词条所列的涌入和隐私义混在同一解释中。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invade"},contexts:[{"domain":"国际新闻","senseId":"invade.s1","en":"The army crossed the border at dawn to invade the neighboring country, while diplomats urged both governments to accept an immediate ceasefire.","zh":"军队在黎明时越过边境入侵邻国，而外交官敦促两国政府立即接受停火。","structure":"while 对照军事行动与外交应对。","grammar":"invade 后接被入侵的国家；urge + object + to-infinitive 表示敦促。","rationale":"此处 invade 表示军队进入他国并试图控制领土，和大批进入或侵犯隐私义不同。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The army invaded the neighboring region before dawn.','军队在黎明前入侵了邻近地区。'),ex(2,'Tourists invade the small harbor each summer.','每年夏天，大批游客涌入这个小港口。'),ex(3,'The newspaper story invaded the actor’s privacy.','这篇报纸报道侵犯了这位演员的隐私。')],mistakes:[m('The army invaded the neighboring country with its permission and without crossing the border.','The army entered the neighboring country with its permission and without crossing the border.','未经许可的武力进入才是军事入侵；获准且未越境不构成 invade。')],quiz:[q('invade',1,1,'An army invades a country when it?','enters by force to take control','leaves after signing a peace treaty','visits with the country’s invitation','军事义 invade 指武力进入一国以夺取控制。'),q('invade',2,2,'Fans invaded the town for the festival. This means they?','arrived there in very large numbers','attacked it with military weapons','left it before the festival began','比喻义 invade 可指大量人群涌入。'),q('invade',3,3,'A report that invades someone’s privacy?','intrudes on their personal life','protects their personal information','asks their permission before publication','invade 可比喻侵犯隐私等个人领域。'),q('invade',4,1,'Which context most clearly has the military sense?','troops crossing a border during a war','visitors entering a museum at opening time','a journalist asking for an interview','战争和军队越境表明军事入侵义。')]});
D('invalid',{etymology:{"origin":"Invalid in the sense not legally effective is analyzed with the negative prefix in- plus valid; the related Latin invalidus meant weak or lacking force.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invalid in the sense not legally effective is analyzed with the negative prefix in- plus valid; the related Latin invalidus meant weak or lacking force."}],"formationLogic":"The legal adjective describes a rule or agreement without binding force; the older Latin form also carried the notion of weakness.","mnemonic":null,"note":"该拼写另有表示病弱者的词条义，本语境和词源说明明确取法律无效义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invalid"},contexts:[{"domain":"合同审查","senseId":"invalid.s1","en":"Because the signature was missing, the lawyer explained that the agreement might be invalid and could not be enforced by the court.","zh":"由于缺少签名，律师解释说这份协议可能无效，法院无法强制执行。","structure":"because 从句给出无效原因，that 从句是 explained 的内容。","grammar":"invalid 作表语形容词；might 表示法律结论仍需审查。","rationale":"invalid 在此表示法律上不生效，而非指久病者或论点缺乏根据。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The contract is invalid because the required signatures are missing.','这份合同无效，因为缺少必要的签名。'),ex(2,'The reviewer rejected the claim as invalid because its figures did not support the conclusion.','审稿人认为这一论断站不住脚，因为数据并不支持结论。'),ex(3,'The novel describes how an invalid depended on his family for daily care.','这部小说描写了一位长期病弱者如何依靠家人照料日常生活。')],mistakes:[m('The court declared the unsigned contract valid and legally ineffective.','The court declared the unsigned contract invalid and legally ineffective.','legally ineffective 与 valid 矛盾；合同缺少签名而无效时应为 invalid。')],quiz:[q('invalid',1,1,'An invalid ticket is?','not legally or officially acceptable','a ticket with an unusually bright color','a ticket that has already been checked successfully','invalid 可指法律或规则上无效的。'),q('invalid',2,2,'An invalid argument is one that?','is not supported by sound facts or reasoning','has been proven beyond any doubt','uses a particularly short sentence','论证义 invalid 指事实或推理站不住脚。'),q('invalid',3,3,'In older usage, an invalid may refer to?','a person who is chronically ill and needs care','a document with a missing signature','a person who checks tickets at a station','invalid 作名词是较旧用法，指久病、体弱的人。'),q('invalid',4,1,'The form was invalidated by a missing signature. Its status became?','without legal effect','more valuable than before','valid for every purpose','无效文件不具备相应法律效力。')]});
D('invaluable',{etymology:{"origin":"Invaluable combines valuable with the intensifying prefix in- in the sense too valuable to estimate; the word is recorded from the eighteenth century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invaluable combines valuable with the intensifying prefix in- in the sense too valuable to estimate; the word is recorded from the eighteenth century."}],"formationLogic":"Here in- does not negate value: it heightens value beyond ordinary measurement.","mnemonic":null,"note":"特别注明 in- 在此非否定前缀，防止误读成“无价值”。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invaluable"},contexts:[{"domain":"研究资源","senseId":"invaluable.s1","en":"The archive’s handwritten field notes proved invaluable to the climate team because they recorded local rainfall before any electronic station existed.","zh":"档案中的手写野外记录对气候团队极其宝贵，因为电子气象站出现前，它们就记录了当地降雨情况。","structure":"because 从句说明资料无可替代的原因，before 引出记录早于设备存在的时间。","grammar":"prove + adjective 表示证明是某种状态；invaluable 作表语形容词。","rationale":"invaluable 表示极有用或重要，早期原意是价值高到难以估价，不是毫无价值。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The local guide proved invaluable when the hikers lost the marked trail.','徒步者迷失在标记路线外时，当地向导发挥了极大的作用。'),ex(2,'The archive preserves invaluable letters from the early expedition.','档案馆保存着早期探险留下的珍贵信件。')],mistakes:[m('Her invaluable advice was useless, and the team succeeded only after ignoring it.','Her valuable advice was useful, and the team succeeded after following it.','invaluable 指极有用、极宝贵；“无用”与词义冲突。')],quiz:[q('invaluable',1,1,'An invaluable source is?','extremely useful or important','of no practical use','easy to replace at any moment','invaluable 表示极有价值或有用。'),q('invaluable',2,2,'Calling an heirloom invaluable suggests that?','its worth is beyond a simple price','it has no value at all','it must be sold immediately','invaluable 常强调珍贵到难以估价，并非毫无价值。'),q('invaluable',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','invaluable experience','invaluableless experience','an invaluable of experience','invaluable 可直接作形容词修饰 experience。'),q('invaluable',4,1,'A witness’s help was invaluable to the inquiry. It was?','essentially helpful','a serious obstacle','not connected with the inquiry','invaluable 的常见用法是形容帮助非常有用。')]});
D('invariably',{etymology:{"origin":"Invariably is the regular adverb from invariable plus -ly; invariable combines in- with variable to mean not changing.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invariably is the regular adverb from invariable plus -ly; invariable combines in- with variable to mean not changing."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective’s fixed-or-unchanging sense passes into an adverb describing actions that occur on every occasion.","mnemonic":null,"note":"来源为透明派生；不把它误拆成表示否定的 in-，其词干构形需按词源分别理解。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invariable"},contexts:[{"domain":"日常习惯","senseId":"invariably.s1","en":"Whenever the laboratory receives a damaged sample, Dr. Chen invariably photographs the packaging before opening it or transferring any material.","zh":"每当实验室收到受损样本，陈博士总会在打开包装或转移任何材料前先拍照。","structure":"whenever 从句表示反复条件，before 短语规定拍照先于操作。","grammar":"invariably 修饰 photographs，表示每次都如此；before 后并列两个动名词。","rationale":"invariably 表示没有例外地总是，句子说明稳定重复的实验记录习惯。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The night bus invariably arrives a few minutes after midnight.','夜班车总是在午夜后几分钟到达。'),ex(2,'The two samples remained invariably the same size under repeated tests.','反复测试下，这两个样本的大小始终不变。')],mistakes:[m('He invariably arrives on time, although he is late for every single meeting.','He frequently arrives late, although he is on time for most meetings.','invariably 表示每次都如此；每次迟到不能同时说明总是准时。')],quiz:[q('invariably',1,1,'If a machine invariably stops at noon, it stops?','every time at noon','only once at noon','at a different time on each day','invariably 表示总是、无一例外。'),q('invariably',2,2,'The readings remained invariably constant. They?','did not change','changed sharply each time','were never recorded','第二义强调状态始终保持不变。'),q('invariably',3,1,'Which adverb is closest in meaning?','always','occasionally','rarely','invariably 可近似解释为 always。'),q('invariably',4,1,'Which sentence uses invariably naturally?','She invariably checks the lock before leaving.','She invariably checked the lock one time only.','She is invariably a lock yesterday.','invariably 修饰动作，表示每次或总是这样。')]});
D('invasion',{etymology:{"origin":"Invasion came through Old French or directly from Latin invasionem, a noun of action from invadere, to attack or enter.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invasion came through Old French or directly from Latin invasionem, a noun of action from invadere, to attack or enter."}],"formationLogic":"The action noun names the act of entering a place by force, following the verb invade.","mnemonic":null,"note":"来源链的中间语言有法语或直接拉丁语两种说法，保留两种可能。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invasion"},contexts:[{"domain":"历史研究","senseId":"invasion.s1","en":"The invasion began before sunrise, and the museum’s maps show how quickly the troops advanced from the coast toward the capital.","zh":"入侵行动在日出前开始，博物馆的地图显示军队如何迅速从海岸推进到首都方向。","structure":"and 连接事件时间与地图展示内容，how 引导 show 的宾语从句。","grammar":"invasion 作名词指武装进入某地；from...toward... 描写推进路线。","rationale":"该词使用武装入侵义，军事背景和 troops 直接对应。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The invasion forced thousands of families to flee across the border.','入侵迫使数千户家庭逃往边境另一侧。')],mistakes:[m('The invasion was peaceful because no army entered the territory and no force was used.','The visit was peaceful because no army entered the territory and no force was used.','invasion 指武装进入某地；没有军队和武力时应改为 visit。')],quiz:[q('invasion',1,1,'An invasion usually involves?','an armed force entering a place','a small group arriving for a picnic','a peaceful exchange of letters','invasion 常指武装力量入侵。'),q('invasion',2,1,'A history of an invasion would describe?','troops entering and attacking a territory','a routine election with no conflict','an ordinary visit to a museum','军事史中的 invasion 是军队入侵。'),q('invasion',3,1,'Which verb is related to invasion?','invade','invent','invert','invasion 是 invade 的名词形式。'),q('invasion',4,1,'After the invasion, the occupied region was controlled by?','the force that entered it','the original local council only','a group of visiting tourists','入侵后通常由入侵力量控制该地区。')]});
D('invent',{etymology:{"origin":"Invent came from Latin inventus, past participle of invenire, to come upon or find, from in- and venire, to come; its earlier English sense was discover.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invent came from Latin inventus, past participle of invenire, to come upon or find, from in- and venire, to come; its earlier English sense was discover."}],"formationLogic":"The sense shifted from finding something to devising something new.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁词源的表面意思是“发现”，现代发明义是后续演变。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invent"},contexts:[{"domain":"技术创新","senseId":"invent.s1","en":"The engineers invented a compact filter that removes lead from well water without electricity, then tested it in three villages.","zh":"工程师发明了一种无需电力即可去除井水中铅的紧凑型过滤器，然后在三个村庄进行了测试。","structure":"that 从句说明过滤器功能，then 连接设计完成后的测试步骤。","grammar":"invent 后接新设计的物品；without electricity 表示过滤器的运行条件。","rationale":"invent 指设计或创造此前不存在的新装置，句中随后进行实地测试。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A young engineer invented a low-cost filter for village wells.','一位年轻工程师发明了一种供乡村水井使用的低成本过滤器。'),ex(2,'The witness admitted that he had invented the story about the missing keys.','证人承认，钥匙失踪的故事是他编造的。')],mistakes:[m('She invented the ancient diary by quoting its exact pages from a verified museum archive.','She copied the ancient diary by quoting its exact pages from a verified museum archive.','从有据可查的档案逐字引用是复制已有材料，不是 invent 新事物或编造故事。')],quiz:[q('invent',1,1,'An engineer invents a device when she?','creates a device that did not exist before','repairs an old device without changing it','borrows a device and returns it','invent 的创造义是设计出以前不存在的东西。'),q('invent',2,2,'If a child invents an excuse, the child?','makes up something that is not true','builds a new machine','finds a true fact in a record','invent 也可指编造不真实的说法。'),q('invent',3,1,'Which noun is formed from invent?','invention','inventory','intervention','invention 是 invent 的名词形式。'),q('invent',4,2,'Which sentence uses invent in the “make up” sense?','He invented a reason for missing class.','She invented a new safety latch.','They patented the invented tool.','invent a reason 指编造理由。')]});
D('invention',{etymology:{"origin":"Invention came from Old French invencion and Latin inventionem, originally finding or discovery, from invenire, to come upon or devise, formed from in- and venire, come.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invention came from Old French invencion and Latin inventionem, originally finding or discovery, from invenire, to come upon or devise, formed from in- and venire, come."}],"formationLogic":"The noun shifted from discovering something to the process and product of creating something new.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁语的较早含义偏向发现；现代器物义是后续发展。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invention"},contexts:[{"domain":"工程与发明","senseId":"invention.s1","en":"The invention of a low-cost water sensor allowed village clinics to detect contamination before patients began showing symptoms.","zh":"这种低成本水质传感器的发明，使村庄诊所能够在患者出现症状前发现污染。","structure":"allowed 引出发明带来的能力，before 从句说明检测早于症状出现。","grammar":"the invention of a sensor 指传感器这一新器物的发明；allow + object + to-infinitive。","rationale":"invention 指以前不存在的新东西，后文说明它解决了何种实际问题。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The invention of the printing press transformed how books were produced.','印刷机的发明改变了书籍的生产方式。')],mistakes:[m('The invention is a newly created device, but it was copied unchanged from a product made centuries earlier.','The invention is a copied device, based unchanged on a product made centuries earlier.','新发明强调创造出新事物；完全照搬数百年前的产品不符合这一意思。')],quiz:[q('invention',1,1,'An invention is?','something new that has been created','a natural object that has never been changed','a list of items in a storeroom','invention 指新发明出来的事物或发明行为。'),q('invention',2,1,'The invention of the telephone refers to?','the act of creating it for the first time','a telephone directory’s inventory','the first telephone interview','the invention of something 指其发明过程。'),q('invention',3,1,'Which person is most directly associated with an invention?','the person who designed and created it','the person who only borrowed it','the person who ignored it','发明者创造了该项 invention。'),q('invention',4,1,'Which phrase is a natural collocation?','a useful invention','an inventation','an inventive of invention','a useful invention 是自然搭配。')]});
D('inventive',{etymology:{"origin":"Inventive entered through Old French inventif from the Latin past-participle stem invent- of invenire, to devise, discover, or find.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Inventive entered through Old French inventif from the Latin past-participle stem invent- of invenire, to devise, discover, or find."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective first described skill in invention and now characterizes people, ideas, or solutions that are resourceful.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 直接把 inventive 联系到 invent-，不另拆出 -ive 的拉丁词源。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inventive"},contexts:[{"domain":"产品设计","senseId":"inventive.s1","en":"An inventive mechanic built a foot-powered pump from spare bicycle parts, giving the remote clinic a reliable source of clean water.","zh":"一位有创造力的机械师用多余的自行车零件造出脚踏水泵，为偏远诊所提供了可靠的清洁水源。","structure":"giving 分词短语说明制作水泵的实际结果。","grammar":"inventive 修饰 mechanic；build A from B 表示用材料制成器物。","rationale":"inventive 表示善于构思新办法，使用旧零件解决缺水问题体现创造力。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The inventive designer turned discarded fabric into durable shopping bags.','这位有创造力的设计师把废弃布料做成了耐用购物袋。')],mistakes:[m('The inventive designer copied every part of an existing product and proposed no new idea.','The unoriginal designer copied every part of an existing product and proposed no new idea.','inventive 表示善于创造新想法；完全照抄且没有新点子应称 unoriginal。')],quiz:[q('inventive',1,1,'An inventive person is good at?','developing new ideas or things','repeating instructions without change','avoiding every kind of problem','inventive 指有创造力、善于想出新办法。'),q('inventive',2,1,'An inventive solution is likely to be?','clever and original','copied without any alteration','impossible to explain or use','inventive solution 往往巧妙且新颖。'),q('inventive',3,1,'Which word is closest in meaning?','creative','routine','unimaginative','inventive 与 creative 意思接近。'),q('inventive',4,1,'Choose the correct sentence.','The team found an inventive way to reuse the water.','The team inventoried way to reuse the water.','The team was inventively idea to reuse the water.','inventive 作形容词修饰 way，表示办法有创意。')]});
D('inventory',{etymology:{"origin":"Inventory came through Old French inventoire from Medieval Latin inventorium, an altered form of Late Latin inventarium, a list of what is found, from inventus of invenire.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Inventory came through Old French inventoire from Medieval Latin inventorium, an altered form of Late Latin inventarium, a list of what is found, from inventus of invenire."}],"formationLogic":"The word names a catalogue of goods by extending the older idea of a record of things found or accounted for.","mnemonic":null,"note":"历史拼写受到 -orium 类词形影响；不把 inventory 错解为 invention 的同义词。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inventory"},contexts:[{"domain":"仓储管理","senseId":"inventory.s1","en":"Before closing the shop for renovation, the owner counted every item in the inventory and recorded which boxes needed replacement labels.","zh":"店主在商店装修停业前清点了库存清单中的每件商品，并记录哪些箱子需要更换标签。","structure":"before 从句说明盘点时间，which 从句是 recorded 的宾语内容。","grammar":"the inventory 指商品清单；count every item 与 record which boxes 是并列动作。","rationale":"inventory 在此指详尽的商品清单，清点和更新标签是清单管理的一部分。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The warehouse manager checked the inventory against the delivery records.','仓库经理对照送货记录核对了库存清单。'),ex(2,'The store reduced its inventory before moving to a smaller building.','商店搬到更小的建筑前减少了库存。'),ex(3,'Each summer, volunteers inventory the equipment in the community center.','每年夏天，志愿者都会清点社区中心的设备。')],mistakes:[m('The store’s inventory lists every product, but none of the listed goods are actually in stock.','The store’s inventory is out of date because none of the listed goods are actually in stock.','inventory 可以是货物清单或库存；若列出的物品都不在仓库，说明清单已过时。')],quiz:[q('inventory',1,1,'A warehouse inventory is?','a detailed list of the goods kept there','a plan showing the building’s exterior color','a record of employees’ birthdays only','inventory 可指对场所物品逐项列出的清单。'),q('inventory',2,2,'A shop has a large inventory of coats. It has?','many coats in stock','a list of coats but none for sale','many customers but no products','inventory 也指商店现有的全部存货。'),q('inventory',3,3,'To inventory the equipment is to?','make a complete list of it','repair every item immediately','sell it without recording anything','inventory 作动词表示逐项清点、列清单。'),q('inventory',4,2,'Which phrase refers to actual goods available for sale?','the shop’s inventory of shoes','an inventory form with no items','a list of last year’s customers','库存义 inventory 指商店持有的实际货物。')]});
D('inverse',{etymology:{"origin":"Inverse came from Latin inversus, turned upside down or reversed, the past participle of invertere, to turn about.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Inverse came from Latin inversus, turned upside down or reversed, the past participle of invertere, to turn about."}],"formationLogic":"The adjective and noun retain the idea of a reversed order or relation.","mnemonic":null,"note":"此例取数学中反函数的基础逆向关系义。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inverse"},contexts:[{"domain":"数学关系","senseId":"inverse.s1","en":"For this one-to-one function, the inverse maps each output back to the unique input that produced it.","zh":"对于这个一一对应函数，反函数会把每个输出映射回产生它的唯一输入。","structure":"that 从句修饰 input，说明输入与输出之间的对应关系。","grammar":"inverse 作名词，指把映射反向的函数；each 与单数 maps 一致。","rationale":"inverse 表示顺序或作用相反，函数把输出还原为输入，体现反向关系。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The relationship between price and demand appeared inverse: as one rose, the other fell.','价格与需求的关系似乎相反：一个上升时，另一个下降。')],mistakes:[m('The two measurements changed in the same direction, showing an inverse relationship.','The two measurements changed in opposite directions, showing an inverse relationship.','inverse relationship 指方向相反；两项指标同向变化不符合此描述。')],quiz:[q('inverse',1,1,'An inverse relationship between two values means?','one tends to move oppositely as the other changes','both always increase together','neither value can ever change','inverse 可指顺序或效果相反的关系。'),q('inverse',2,1,'The inverse of a usual order is?','the order turned the other way around','the same order repeated','a list without any items','inverse 表示通常关系或顺序的反向。'),q('inverse',3,1,'Which pair is most likely inverse in the described case?','one rises while the other falls','both rise at exactly the same time','both remain fixed forever','一升一降体现相反方向。'),q('inverse',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','an inverse relationship','an inversely relationship','an inversion relationship of opposite','inverse 可作形容词修饰 relationship。')]});
D('invert',{etymology:{"origin":"Invert came from Latin invertere, to turn about or reverse, from in- and vertere, to turn.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invert came from Latin invertere, to turn about or reverse, from in- and vertere, to turn."}],"formationLogic":"The literal turning-around sense continues in both physical and more abstract uses.","mnemonic":null,"note":"拉丁构词和物理倒置义对应明确。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invert"},contexts:[{"domain":"食品包装","senseId":"invert.s1","en":"Before pouring the sauce, invert the sealed bottle twice so the settled herbs mix evenly through the liquid.","zh":"倒出酱汁前，把密封瓶倒转两次，让沉淀的香草均匀混入液体。","structure":"before 短语规定动作顺序，so 引出倒转瓶子的目的。","grammar":"invert 是及物动词，瓶子作宾语；so 后省略重复主语。","rationale":"invert 表示把物体翻转，使原来的上方转到下方。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Invert the bottle over the sink to drain the last drops.','把瓶子倒过来放在水槽上方，让最后几滴流出来。'),ex(2,'The editor inverted the usual order of the chapters.','编辑把章节的通常顺序颠倒了。')],mistakes:[m('She inverted the cup by placing it upright on the table with its opening facing upward.','She placed the cup upright on the table with its opening facing upward.','invert 指倒置或反转；杯口朝上直立摆放不是倒置。')],quiz:[q('invert',1,1,'To invert a bottle is to?','turn it upside down','fill it without moving it','remove its label','invert 的基本义是把物体上下倒置。'),q('invert',2,2,'If a writer inverts the usual order, the writer?','reverses the order','copies it exactly','removes every chapter','invert 也可指把惯常次序反过来。'),q('invert',3,1,'Which action would invert a glass?','turning it upside down','putting it beside another glass','washing it with warm water','invert a glass 是把杯子倒过来。'),q('invert',4,2,'The analyst inverted the usual cause-and-effect order. The analyst?','reversed the expected relationship','confirmed it without change','removed all evidence','invert 可用于反转关系或通常顺序。')]});
D('invest',{etymology:{"origin":"Invest came from Latin investire, to clothe or cover, from in- and vestis, clothing; the financial sense developed later from the notion of committing or placing resources.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Invest came from Latin investire, to clothe or cover, from in- and vestis, clothing; the financial sense developed later from the notion of committing or placing resources."}],"formationLogic":"The older clothing metaphor broadened to the act of putting money into an enterprise or asset.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline records both the literal clothing source and later financial sense; here no literal garment is implied.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invest"},contexts:[{"domain":"创业融资","senseId":"invest.s1","en":"The cooperative decided to invest part of its reserve in refrigerated storage, expecting the equipment to reduce food waste over several years.","zh":"合作社决定把部分储备金投资于冷藏仓储设施，预计这些设备能在几年内减少食物浪费。","structure":"expecting 分词短语补充投资的预期收益。","grammar":"invest money in something 是投资搭配；expect + object + to-infinitive 表预期。","rationale":"invest 在此指投入资金以获得未来收益，具体用途为冷藏设备。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The fund invested in renewable energy projects across three regions.','该基金投资了三个地区的可再生能源项目。'),ex(2,'She invested months of careful work in the translation.','她在这份译文中投入了几个月的细致工作。'),ex(3,'The council invested the new director with authority to approve grants.','委员会授予新主任批准拨款的权力。'),ex(4,'A layer of mist invested the hillside at dawn.','黎明时，薄雾笼罩着山坡。')],mistakes:[m('He invested money in the company, but put no money into it and bought no shares.','He became interested in the company, but put no money into it and bought no shares.','前半句明确说投入资金，后半句却说没有投入资金或购买股份，彼此矛盾。')],quiz:[q('invest',1,1,'To invest money in a company is to?','put money into it in expectation of a return','borrow money from it without agreement','write a review about it','invest 的金融义是为获利把资金投入企业或财产。'),q('invest',2,2,'She invested considerable time in training. She?','devoted time and effort to it','received a cash dividend from it','avoided spending any time on it','invest time/effort 表示投入时间或精力。'),q('invest',3,3,'A formal ceremony invested him with authority. It?','gave him authority officially','took every power away','asked him to make a private donation','invest someone with power 表示正式授予权力。'),q('invest',4,4,'In literary usage, fog invested the valley. Fog?','surrounded or covered the valley','bought the valley as property','measured the valley’s width','书面义 invest 可表示像衣物一样笼罩、包围。')]});
D('investigate',{etymology:{"origin":"Investigate came from Latin investigare, to track or trace out, from in- and vestigium, a footprint or track.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Investigate came from Latin investigare, to track or trace out, from in- and vestigium, a footprint or track."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin image of following tracks developed into a careful search for facts or causes.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Etymonline 把词根联系到 vestigium 脚印；这解释追踪线索的概念。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/investigate"},contexts:[{"domain":"事故调查","senseId":"investigate.s1","en":"Engineers investigated the bridge failure by comparing maintenance logs with photographs taken immediately after the storm.","zh":"工程师通过将维护日志与风暴后立即拍摄的照片进行对照，调查了桥梁坍塌原因。","structure":"by comparing 说明调查方法，taken 短语修饰 photographs。","grammar":"investigate 后接被调查的事件；compare A with B 表示比较两类证据。","rationale":"investigate 指仔细查明事故事实，日志和照片是调查材料。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Police are investigating whether the alarm failed before the fire started.','警方正在调查火灾发生前警报是否失灵。'),ex(2,'The team investigated how different soils affect seed growth.','团队研究了不同土壤如何影响种子生长。')],mistakes:[m('The committee investigated the complaint by refusing to read the evidence or speak to witnesses.','The committee ignored the complaint by refusing to read the evidence or speak to witnesses.','investigate 要查明事实；拒绝查看证据和询问证人是忽视问题，而非调查。')],quiz:[q('investigate',1,1,'Police investigate a burglary in order to?','find out the facts about what happened','decide the verdict before collecting evidence','repair the broken window only','investigate crime 是调查事实。'),q('investigate',2,2,'Scientists investigate a question when they?','study it carefully to learn more','assume the answer without testing','hide the results from themselves','investigate 也指系统研究问题。'),q('investigate',3,1,'Which construction is standard?','investigate the cause','investigate into the cause','investigate to the cause','investigate 可直接接宾语，通常不加 into。'),q('investigate',4,2,'A researcher investigating seed growth would likely?','observe and compare how seeds develop','arrest the seeds for a crime','interview the soil about its salary','研究者 investigate 是仔细研究生长情况。')]});
D('investigation',{etymology:{"origin":"Investigation came from Latin investigationem, a noun of action from investigare, to track or trace out, from vestigium, a footprint.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Investigation came from Latin investigationem, a noun of action from investigare, to track or trace out, from vestigium, a footprint."}],"formationLogic":"The noun names the systematic process of following clues until facts can be established.","mnemonic":null,"note":"来源说明与 investigate 同族，但该名词有独立拉丁名词后缀历史。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/investigation"},contexts:[{"domain":"公共安全","senseId":"investigation.s1","en":"The investigation found no evidence that the alarm had failed, but it recommended replacing the battery before the next inspection.","zh":"调查没有发现警报器失灵的证据，但建议在下次检查前更换电池。","structure":"but 转折引出预防性建议，that 从句补充未找到的证据内容。","grammar":"investigation 作名词指查找事实的过程；recommend + gerund 表示建议做某事。","rationale":"该词表示对事故或问题事实进行仔细核查，最终结论和建议体现过程。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The investigation uncovered several errors in the safety inspection records.','调查发现安全检查记录中有几处错误。')],mistakes:[m('The team called it a thorough investigation, although it never examined records or interviewed anyone.','The team called it an incomplete inquiry because it never examined records or interviewed anyone.','不看记录也不询问任何人，不能称为 thorough investigation；调查并未充分开展。')],quiz:[q('investigation',1,1,'An investigation is a careful effort to?','find facts about a problem or event','design a new product for sale','make a list of vacation dates','investigation 指对问题或事件查明事实的调查。'),q('investigation',2,1,'A police investigation may include?','examining evidence and interviewing witnesses','choosing a verdict before examining anything','closing the case without collecting facts','调查包括收集证据和访问证人。'),q('investigation',3,1,'Which verb is closely related to investigation?','investigate','invent','invert','investigation 是 investigate 的名词形式。'),q('investigation',4,1,'The investigation is ongoing. This means it is?','still in progress','finished before it began','unrelated to any inquiry','ongoing investigation 表示调查仍在进行。')]});
D('investment',{etymology:{"origin":"Investment is the noun from invest plus -ment; invest came from Latin investire, to clothe, with the financial sense later applied to committed resources.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Investment is the noun from invest plus -ment; invest came from Latin investire, to clothe, with the financial sense later applied to committed resources."}],"formationLogic":"The suffix names the act or resulting sum of committing capital to an asset or project.","mnemonic":null,"note":"词源说明保留衣着词源与现代金融义间的历史语义变化。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/investment"},contexts:[{"domain":"个人理财","senseId":"investment.s1","en":"The investment in rooftop insulation paid for itself over five winters because the household spent much less on heating.","zh":"屋顶保温方面的投资在五个冬天内收回了成本，因为这户人家少花了很多取暖费。","structure":"because 从句说明成本收回的原因，over five winters 表示时间范围。","grammar":"investment 作名词指投入并期待收益的钱；pay for itself 表示收回成本。","rationale":"此处 investment 是资金投入项目，不是穿衣或授予职位等历史相关义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The railway project requires a large investment before it can serve remote towns.','这项铁路工程在服务偏远城镇之前需要大量投资。')],mistakes:[m('The company made an investment but put no money, time, or resources into the project.','The company made no investment because it put no money, time, or resources into the project.','investment 表示投入资金或资源；完全没有投入却说作了投资，前后矛盾。')],quiz:[q('investment',1,1,'An investment is money or resources put into something in order to?','gain a future benefit or return','ensure that nothing can ever change','avoid making any commitment','investment 通常是期待未来收益而投入的资金或资源。'),q('investment',2,1,'A government investment in railways may pay off through?','better transport and future economic benefits','a guaranteed immediate profit in every case','the disappearance of every travel need','公共基础设施投资可能带来长期收益。'),q('investment',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','a long-term investment','an investation','an investmented','long-term investment 是常见搭配。'),q('investment',4,1,'The new equipment was a worthwhile investment. This suggests it?','was worth the resources spent on it','was never purchased or used','made the company avoid all costs','worthwhile investment 表示所投入的资源值得。')]});
D('investments',{etymology:{"origin":"Investments is the regular plural of investment, formed from invest with the noun suffix -ment; invest’s English financial sense developed from the older Latin verb for clothing or covering.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Investments is the regular plural of investment, formed from invest with the noun suffix -ment; invest’s English financial sense developed from the older Latin verb for clothing or covering."}],"formationLogic":"The plural counts separate allocations or holdings made with the aim of future returns.","mnemonic":null,"note":"复数词形不另造词源；其基础 investment 见同一词族。","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/investment"},contexts:[{"domain":"资产配置","senseId":"investments.s1","en":"Her investments are spread across savings bonds and two small businesses, which reduces the risk of relying on one source of income.","zh":"她的投资分散在储蓄债券和两家小企业中，这降低了只依赖一种收入来源的风险。","structure":"which 从句说明分散投资产生的效果。","grammar":"investments 是 investment 的规则复数；are spread across 表示分布于多个资产类别。","rationale":"复数 investments 指多笔或多项投资，句中列出三类资金配置。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her investments include shares, government bonds, and a small rental property.','她的投资包括股票、政府债券和一处小型出租房产。')],mistakes:[m('His investments were all sold last year, and he has not repurchased them, but he still owns every one today.','His investments were all sold last year, and he has not repurchased them, so he no longer owns them today.','明确说明没有重新买回后，仍声称持有所有投资品就与已售出相矛盾。')],quiz:[q('investments',1,1,'A person’s investments are?','assets or amounts of money they have put into things','only the unpaid bills they owe','a record of all their favorite songs','investments 是 invest 的复数，指投入的款项或资产。'),q('investments',2,1,'If someone says their investments paid off, the investments?','produced a useful return or benefit','were never made','caused every asset to disappear','investments paid off 表示投资取得了回报。'),q('investments',3,1,'Which item could be one of a person’s investments?','shares in a company','a weather forecast','a borrowed library card','股票可以是个人投资组合中的一项资产。'),q('investments',4,1,'A portfolio of investments is a collection of?','assets held for investment','unrelated recipes','public road signs','investment portfolio 指投资资产的组合。')]});
D('invigorate',{etymology:{"origin":"Recorded in the 1640s from in- (here ‘in/toward’), vigor, and -ate; an earlier form was envigor, from Old French envigorer.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Recorded in the 1640s from in- (here ‘in/toward’), vigor, and -ate; an earlier form was envigor, from Old French envigorer."}],"formationLogic":"The formation means to put vigor into someone or something; here it describes renewed energy after exertion.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The initial in- is not the negative prefix here; it contributes the sense ‘in/toward’.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invigorate"},contexts:[{"domain":"Well-being","senseId":"invigorate.s1","en":"A brisk walk around the block invigorated the volunteers, and they returned to the cleanup with enough energy to finish the heavy work.","zh":"绕街区快走一圈让志愿者们重新振作起来，他们回来后精力充沛，足以完成繁重的工作。","structure":"A brisk walk around the block (subject) + invigorated (verb) + the volunteers (object); the following and-clause shows the result.","grammar":"及物动词；invigorate + 人/身体等，表示使恢复精力。","rationale":"with enough energy... makes the result of invigorated concrete; the word describes renewed energy, not merely a pleasant mood.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A brisk walk in the cool air invigorated the tired hikers.','凉爽空气中的快步行走让疲惫的徒步者恢复了精神。')],mistakes:[m('The refreshing break invigorated the team, leaving everyone more exhausted and less alert.','The refreshing break invigorated the team, leaving everyone more energetic and alert.','invigorate 意为使恢复精力；更加疲惫、迟钝与之相反。')],quiz:[q('invigorate',1,1,'A short rest invigorates someone when it?','restores their energy and strength','makes them weaker and more tired','removes their ability to move','invigorate 表示使人振奋、恢复精力。'),q('invigorate',2,1,'A cool swim may invigorate you by making you feel?','refreshed and more energetic','sleepier than before','unable to recognize water','invigorate 可描述令人精神一振。'),q('invigorate',3,1,'Which verb is closest in meaning?','energize','exhaust','weaken','energize 是 invigorate 的近义表达。'),q('invigorate',4,1,'Choose the natural sentence.','The fresh air invigorated us.','The fresh air was invigorating us to tiredness.','The fresh air invigorated of us.','invigorate 可直接接人作宾语，表示使其精力充沛。')]});
D('inviolable',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin inviolabilis: negative in- + violabilis, ‘that may be violated,’ from violare ‘do violence to’; the English word is recorded by the mid-15th century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin inviolabilis: negative in- + violabilis, ‘that may be violated,’ from violare ‘do violence to’; the English word is recorded by the mid-15th century."}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix reverses ‘liable to violation’: an inviolable right or rule must not be violated.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The historical source supports the Latin elements; no further root claim is needed.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inviolable"},contexts:[{"domain":"Law and ethics","senseId":"inviolable.s1","en":"The agreement treats each patient's medical privacy as inviolable, so staff may disclose records only when the patient consents or the law requires it.","zh":"协议将每位患者的医疗隐私视为不可侵犯，因此工作人员只有在患者同意或法律要求时才能披露记录。","structure":"The agreement treats + object + as + complement; the so-clause states the practical consequence of that status.","grammar":"形容词作宾语补足语；inviolable 表示必须遵守、不得侵犯。","rationale":"Only when introduces the narrow exceptions, clarifying that inviolable describes a protected principle rather than an ordinary preference.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The constitution describes the right to a fair hearing as inviolable.','宪法将获得公平听证的权利规定为不可侵犯。')],mistakes:[m('The inviolable rule was routinely broken whenever it became inconvenient.','The flexible rule was routinely changed whenever it became inconvenient.','inviolable 表示不容侵犯或破坏；若规则经常被打破，就不符合此义。')],quiz:[q('inviolable',1,1,'An inviolable right is one that?','must not be violated or taken away','can be ignored whenever convenient','exists only for one day','inviolable 指不可侵犯、不容破坏的。'),q('inviolable',2,1,'A principle described as inviolable is treated as?','sacred or beyond violation','optional and easily discarded','a temporary suggestion','inviolable 常强调原则不可触犯。'),q('inviolable',3,1,'Which phrase is most natural?','inviolable human rights','inviolablely human rights','an inviolable of rights','inviolable 可作形容词修饰 human rights。'),q('inviolable',4,1,'If a boundary is inviolable, others must?','respect it and not cross it','erase it whenever they wish','change it every morning','inviolable 的意思包含不容侵犯。')]});
D('invisible',{etymology:{"origin":"Via Old French invisible from Latin invisibilis, negative in- + visibilis ‘visible’; related to Latin videre ‘to see.’","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Via Old French invisible from Latin invisibilis, negative in- + visibilis ‘visible’; related to Latin videre ‘to see.’"}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix marks something as not visible; this context uses the literal visual sense.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The Latin family is supported; the note avoids claiming that every hidden or unnoticed thing is literally invisible.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invisible"},contexts:[{"domain":"Science and safety","senseId":"invisible.s1","en":"Carbon monoxide is invisible and has no smell, which is why a working detector is essential even when a room seems perfectly safe.","zh":"一氧化碳看不见也没有气味，所以即使房间看起来完全安全，正常工作的探测器仍然必不可少。","structure":"Subject + linking verb + two coordinated adjectives; which is why introduces the consequence.","grammar":"系动词 is 后接并列形容词作表语；invisible 指肉眼无法看见。","rationale":"The smell clause separates visibility from odor, while the detector explains why an invisible hazard can still be present.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The tiny spores are invisible without a microscope.','不用显微镜就看不见这些微小孢子。'),ex(2,'The unpaid work of caregivers often remains invisible in official statistics.','照护者的无偿劳动常常没有体现在官方统计中。')],mistakes:[m('The invisible ink was clearly visible to the naked eye in bright red.','The visible ink was clearly visible to the naked eye in bright red.','肉眼可见的鲜红墨水与 invisible 相矛盾；此处应改为 visible。')],quiz:[q('invisible',1,1,'Bacteria invisible to the naked eye are?','too small to be seen without help','colored bright red and easy to see','hidden only because they are underground','invisible 可指肉眼看不见的。'),q('invisible',2,2,'A worker whose contributions remain invisible is?','present but not noticed or recognized','physically impossible to see','the only person in the building','比喻义 invisible 可表示存在却不被注意或认可。'),q('invisible',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','invisible to the naked eye','invisible for the naked eye','invisible at naked eye','常用结构是 invisible to the naked eye。'),q('invisible',4,2,'If a problem is invisible to the public, it may still?','exist even though people do not notice it','be impossible to exist anywhere','be visible in every public report','引申义强调问题存在但没有受到关注。')]});
D('invitation',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin invitationem, the action noun of invitare ‘invite, treat, entertain’; its first element in- meant ‘toward,’ while the deeper origin of invitare is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin invitationem, the action noun of invitare ‘invite, treat, entertain’; its first element in- meant ‘toward,’ while the deeper origin of invitare is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The noun names the act or message that draws someone toward an event; the Latin verb’s deeper origin is not established here.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The remote origin of invitare is left uncertain rather than supplied with an unsupported root.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invitation"},contexts:[{"domain":"Social life","senseId":"invitation.s1","en":"Maya kept the invitation on her desk until she could check whether her train would arrive before the wedding ceremony began.","zh":"玛雅把请柬留在桌上，直到她确认火车能否在婚礼仪式开始前抵达。","structure":"Main clause + until-clause; whether introduces the indirect question embedded after check.","grammar":"invitation 是名词，指邀请或请柬；whether 引导 check 的间接疑问内容。","rationale":"The sentence distinguishes receiving an invitation from deciding whether the schedule makes attendance possible.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'We received an invitation to attend the opening ceremony.','我们收到了参加开幕式的邀请。')],mistakes:[m('She accepted the invitation, explicitly declined to attend, and said she was accepting it.','She declined the invitation and said she would not attend.','同一句中既接受又明确拒绝同一邀请，前后矛盾；拒绝应说 decline。')],quiz:[q('invitation',1,1,'An invitation asks someone to?','come to an event or place','pay an overdue bill','solve a puzzle alone','invitation 指邀请某人前来的请求或请柬。'),q('invitation',2,1,'A wedding invitation usually tells a guest?','when and where the wedding will take place','how to repair the wedding hall','which person owns the invitation paper','请柬通常告知活动时间地点。'),q('invitation',3,1,'Which verb commonly goes with invitation?','accept','invent','irrigate','accept an invitation 是接受邀请的常用搭配。'),q('invitation',4,1,'Choose the correct plural.','invitations','invitationes','invitation’s','invitation 的复数形式是 invitations。')]});
D('invite',{etymology:{"origin":"Recorded in the 1530s, invite may be a back-formation from invitation or may come through French inviter from Latin invitare; the Latin word's origin is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Recorded in the 1530s, invite may be a back-formation from invitation or may come through French inviter from Latin invitare; the Latin word's origin is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The modern verb invites a person toward an event or activity; its English formation has two proposed routes, so neither is presented as certain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Both proposed pathways are retained; the deeper source of Latin invitare is uncertain.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invite"},contexts:[{"domain":"Events","senseId":"invite.s1","en":"The organizers will invite several local residents to speak at the meeting, but they have not yet decided who will represent the neighborhood.","zh":"组织者将邀请几位当地居民在会上发言，但他们尚未决定由谁代表这个社区。","structure":"Will + verb + object + to-infinitive; the but-clause adds a contrast about the later selection.","grammar":"invite + 人 + to do 表示邀请某人做某事；will 后用动词原形。","rationale":"The context gives invite its event-participation sense and makes clear the invitees are asked to speak.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The neighbors invited us to join their garden party.','邻居邀请我们参加他们的花园聚会。'),ex(2,'The editor invited readers to submit questions before Friday.','编辑请读者在周五前提交问题。'),ex(3,'Leaving the gate open invites unwanted visitors.','大门敞开会招来不速之客。'),ex(4,'He sent us an invite to the launch next month.','他给我们发了下个月发布会的请帖。')],mistakes:[m('The editor invited comments from readers but ordered everyone not to share any opinions.','The editor invited comments from readers and asked them to share their opinions.','invite comments 是征求意见；同时禁止任何人表达意见会抵消邀请的意思。')],quiz:[q('invite',1,1,'They invited Nora to the ceremony. They?','asked her to attend it','asked her to leave before it began','sent her the final report afterward','invite someone to an event 是邀请某人参加。'),q('invite',2,2,'A report that invites comments?','asks readers to give their opinions','rejects every response in advance','records only the editor’s private diary','invite comments 表示征求意见。'),q('invite',3,3,'Leaving food outside may invite trouble. It may?','make trouble more likely','make the food impossible to see','formally ask trouble to attend a meeting','invite trouble 是招致麻烦。'),q('invite',4,4,'In casual speech, an invite is?','an invitation','an invited person','an interview question','invite 可作口语名词，意为请帖或邀请。')]});
D('invitee',{etymology:{"origin":"First recorded in 1837, invitee is formed from invite + -ee; the suffix marks the person who receives an action.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"First recorded in 1837, invitee is formed from invite + -ee; the suffix marks the person who receives an action."}],"formationLogic":"The -ee ending identifies the recipient of inviting: the invitee is the person invited.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The derivation is transparent from the attested English verb and recipient suffix.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invitee"},contexts:[{"domain":"Events","senseId":"invitee.s1","en":"Each invitee received a message with the venue address and a link for confirming attendance by Friday.","zh":"每位受邀者都收到一条消息，其中有场地地址以及一个要求在周五前确认出席的链接。","structure":"Each + singular count noun + singular verb; with-phrase modifies message, and for + -ing states the link's purpose.","grammar":"invitee 是可数名词；each 后用单数谓语。by Friday 表示截止时间。","rationale":"The sentence identifies the invitee as the person receiving an invitation, rather than the person who sends it.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Each invitee received a numbered badge at the entrance.','每位受邀者都在入口处领到一枚带编号的徽章。')],mistakes:[m('The invitee received the invitation and was the person who hosted and sent the same invitation.','The host sent the invitation, and the invitee received it.','invitee 是收到邀请的一方；发出邀请、组织活动的一方是 host。')],quiz:[q('invitee',1,1,'An invitee is the person who?','has been invited','writes every invitation','owns the event venue','invitee 指受到邀请的人。'),q('invitee',2,1,'The invitee confirmed attendance. Who confirmed?','the person who received the invitation','the person who printed the invitation','the person who canceled the event','受邀者确认是否出席。'),q('invitee',3,1,'Which role is the opposite side of an invitee?','host','guest list','invitation card','host 主办或邀请他人，invitee 是受邀者。'),q('invitee',4,1,'Choose the correct plural.','invitees','invitees’','inviteeings','invitee 的复数直接加 s，写作 invitees。')]});
D('involve',{etymology:{"origin":"From Old French and Latin involvere, literally ‘roll into,’ from in- ‘in’ + volvere ‘roll’; the sense ‘include’ is recorded around 1600.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Old French and Latin involvere, literally ‘roll into,’ from in- ‘in’ + volvere ‘roll’; the sense ‘include’ is recorded around 1600."}],"formationLogic":"The older physical image of rolling something in developed into the idea that a task includes certain necessary parts.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The Latin elements and later ‘include’ sense are supported by the source.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/involve"},contexts:[{"domain":"Projects","senseId":"involve.s1","en":"Replacing the old heating system will involve closing two classrooms for a week, so teachers are arranging temporary spaces nearby.","zh":"更换旧供暖系统将需要关闭两间教室一周，因此教师们正在附近安排临时场地。","structure":"Gerund phrase as subject + involve + noun/gerund complement; so introduces the resulting arrangement.","grammar":"及物动词 involve + 名词或动名词，表示某事需要包含某项工作。","rationale":"Closing two classrooms is a necessary part of replacing the system, which anchors involve to its ‘include as a necessary part’ sense.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The repair will involve replacing two damaged pipes.','这次维修需要更换两根损坏的管道。'),ex(2,'The teacher involved every student in planning the science fair.','老师让每位学生都参与科学展的筹备。'),ex(3,'Investigators found no evidence to involve her in the theft.','调查人员没有找到能把她牵涉进盗窃案的证据。')],mistakes:[m('The job involves to travel between several towns each week.','The job involves travelling between several towns each week.','involve 作“需要做某事”时后接动名词，不接 to do。')],quiz:[q('involve',1,1,'A job that involves driving requires the worker to?','drive as part of the work','avoid every vehicle','own the whole transport company','involve doing 表示工作内容需要做某事。'),q('involve',2,2,'To involve children in cooking is to?','let them take part in preparing the food','ask them to leave the kitchen','make the food without their help','involve someone in 表示使其参与。'),q('involve',3,3,'If evidence involves a person in a crime, it?','connects that person with the crime','proves the person was on vacation','removes the crime from the record','involve someone in a crime 表示牵连。'),q('involve',4,1,'Choose the correct pattern.','The plan involves making several calls.','The plan involves to make several calls.','The plan involves make several calls.','动词 involve 后接动名词作宾语。')]});
D('invulnerable',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin invulnerabilis: negative in- + vulnerabilis ‘capable of being wounded,’ related to vulnerare ‘wound’; the deeper origin of the wound-word is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin invulnerabilis: negative in- + vulnerabilis ‘capable of being wounded,’ related to vulnerare ‘wound’; the deeper origin of the wound-word is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix means ‘not vulnerable’; figuratively, something invulnerable cannot be harmed by the stated threat.","mnemonic":null,"note":"Only the supported Latin relationship is given; the remote origin of vulnerare is not asserted.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/invulnerable"},contexts:[{"domain":"Security","senseId":"invulnerable.s1","en":"No password is invulnerable to attack, so the company requires long unique passwords and a second verification step for every account.","zh":"没有任何密码能免受攻击，因此公司要求每个账户使用足够长且独特的密码，并增加第二步验证。","structure":"No + singular noun + be + adjective; the so-clause gives the safeguard that follows from this claim.","grammar":"invulnerable to + 名词表示不受某种伤害或攻击；no 与单数名词连用，表达全称否定。","rationale":"The sentence uses invulnerable figuratively for resistance to harm and immediately avoids the false implication of perfect security.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The fortress was not invulnerable; a narrow breach remained in its eastern wall.','这座堡垒并非坚不可摧；东墙上仍有一处狭窄缺口。')],mistakes:[m('The shield was invulnerable to ordinary blows, yet the first ordinary blow broke it.','The shield was vulnerable to ordinary blows, and the first ordinary blow broke it.','“不受普通攻击伤害”与“被第一下普通攻击打破”直接矛盾。')],quiz:[q('invulnerable',1,1,'An invulnerable character is?','impossible or very difficult to harm','easily injured by every small touch','unwilling to answer a question','invulnerable 表示不受伤害、难以攻破。'),q('invulnerable',2,1,'A team that feels invulnerable may believe it?','cannot be defeated or hurt','has already lost every match','is not allowed to play','引申用法表示觉得自己不会受到伤害或失败。'),q('invulnerable',3,1,'Which preposition commonly follows invulnerable?','to','by at','for with','常用结构是 invulnerable to。'),q('invulnerable',4,1,'A fort that is not invulnerable?','can still be damaged or captured','is certain to resist everything','has no walls at all by definition','not invulnerable 表示仍可能受损。')]});
D('inward',{etymology:{"origin":"Old English inweard combined the word for ‘in’ with -weard ‘-ward, in the direction of’; it also had older senses such as ‘inmost’ and ‘internal.’","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Old English inweard combined the word for ‘in’ with -weard ‘-ward, in the direction of’; it also had older senses such as ‘inmost’ and ‘internal.’"}],"formationLogic":"The direction component remains visible in the modern literal sense: inward means toward the inside.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The Old English components are supported; no later adverbial history is inferred beyond the source.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inward"},contexts:[{"domain":"Architecture","senseId":"inward.s1","en":"The emergency doors open inward, so visitors must keep the landing clear instead of leaving boxes in front of them.","zh":"紧急出口门向内开启，因此访客必须保持平台畅通，不能把箱子堆在门前。","structure":"Subject + open + directional adverb; so introduces a consequence, and instead of + gerund names the alternative to avoid.","grammar":"inward 作方向副词，表示朝里面；open inward 描述门的开启方向。","rationale":"The landing and boxes make the direction operationally important: inward-opening doors need clear interior space.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The door opens inward, so keep the space behind it clear.','这扇门向内开，因此要保持门后空间畅通。'),ex(2,'Despite her outward smile, she felt an inward sadness.','尽管她表面微笑，内心仍感到悲伤。'),ex(3,'After the argument, his thoughts turned inward.','争吵之后，他开始反省自己的内心。')],mistakes:[m('The door opens inward, swinging away from the room and toward the street.','The door opens outward, swinging away from the room and toward the street.','向外摆到街道上应说 opens outward；inward 是朝房间内部。')],quiz:[q('inward',1,1,'An inward curve bends?','toward the inside or center','away from the center','only in a straight line','inward 作形容词或副词可表示朝内。'),q('inward',2,2,'An inward feeling is one that is?','experienced privately in the mind','shown openly on a public sign','located in another country','inward 也可指内心的、精神上的。'),q('inward',3,3,'When someone turns inward, they turn their attention?','toward their own thoughts','toward a distant crowd','toward the nearest exit only','turn inward 是转向内心、反省。'),q('inward',4,1,'Which opposite best contrasts with inward direction?','outward','internal','interior','outward 表示向外，与方向义 inward 相对。')]});
D('inwardly',{etymology:{"origin":"Old English inweardlice; formed from inward + -ly, with inward going back to inweard.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Old English inweardlice; formed from inward + -ly, with inward going back to inweard."}],"formationLogic":"The adverb adds -ly to describe a state experienced internally; the context contrasts that state with visible behavior.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The derivation follows the recorded Old English form and the transparent modern suffix.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inwardly"},contexts:[{"domain":"Emotions","senseId":"inwardly.s1","en":"Although Lin thanked the reviewer calmly, she was inwardly upset by the comment and needed time before responding to it.","zh":"尽管林平静地感谢了审稿人，她内心却因那条评论而难过，需要一些时间再作回应。","structure":"Although-clause contrasts outward behavior with the main clause; inwardly modifies upset.","grammar":"inwardly 是方式副词，修饰形容词 upset，表示内心的状态而非外在表现。","rationale":"The calm thanks and inward upset are deliberately contrasted, making the ‘not shown to others’ sense clear.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'She inwardly disagreed with the proposal but waited for the discussion to end.','她心里不同意这个提议，但等讨论结束后才表态。')],mistakes:[m('He inwardly announced his opinion over the loudspeaker so everyone could hear it.','He openly announced his opinion over the loudspeaker so everyone could hear it.','inwardly 表示内心、不对外表露；通过扩音器让大家听到是公开表达。')],quiz:[q('inwardly',1,1,'If someone inwardly smiles, the smile is?','felt or imagined privately rather than shown','painted on an outside wall','heard by everyone in the room','inwardly 表示在内心里，而非外在显露。'),q('inwardly',2,1,'She inwardly objected but said nothing. What happened?','she disagreed in her mind without expressing it','she shouted her objection to the crowd','she forgot what the discussion concerned','inwardly objected 指内心反对但没有说出来。'),q('inwardly',3,1,'Which adjective is inwardly formed from?','inward','invisible','international','inwardly 是 inward 加 -ly 构成的副词。'),q('inwardly',4,1,'Which phrase is most natural?','inwardly relieved','inward reliefly','inwardly relief','副词 inwardly 可修饰形容词 relieved。')]});
D('inwards',{etymology:{"origin":"The direction word derives from inward; the adverbial form in -s is recorded in English, but this source does not specify the exact history of that ending.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"The direction word derives from inward; the adverbial form in -s is recorded in English, but this source does not specify the exact history of that ending."}],"formationLogic":"In this instruction, inwards marks motion toward the inside; the precise historical development of the final -s is not claimed.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The exact history of adverbial -s is left unspecified rather than guessed.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inwards"},contexts:[{"domain":"Instructions","senseId":"inwards.s1","en":"After the outer latch clicks, slide the small panel inwards until it sits flush with the frame.","zh":"外侧闩锁咔嗒扣上后，将小面板向内滑动，直到它与框架齐平。","structure":"Imperative verb + object + directional adverb; until-clause gives the stopping point.","grammar":"inwards 作方向副词修饰 slide，表示朝内；until 引导动作达到的终点。","rationale":"The frame provides a concrete reference point for the direction, preventing confusion with outward movement.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Fold the loose edges inwards before you tape the parcel.','用胶带封包裹前，先把松散边缘向内折。')],mistakes:[m('Push the door inwards, away from the building and into the street.','Push the door outwards, away from the building and into the street.','远离建筑、朝街道的方向是向外 outwards，不是向内 inwards。')],quiz:[q('inwards',1,1,'To fold a flap inwards is to fold it?','toward the inside','away from the center','along the outside edge only','inwards 是朝里面的方向。'),q('inwards',2,1,'Which word is a common alternative to inwards?','inward','international','interim','inward 可作 inwards 的常见对应形式。'),q('inwards',3,1,'Which instruction uses inwards correctly?','Turn the loose corners inwards.','Turn the loose corners inwards away from the center.','Turn the loose corners inwards outside the box.','inwards 要描述朝里折或转的方向。'),q('inwards',4,1,'Inwards is especially common in which variety?','British English','only ancient Greek','American sign language only','inwards 是英式英语中常见的副词形式。')]});
D('iris',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin iris, from Greek iris ‘rainbow’; the Greek word's deeper origin is uncertain, though it traditionally has been connected with a root meaning ‘bend or turn.’","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin iris, from Greek iris ‘rainbow’; the Greek word's deeper origin is uncertain, though it traditionally has been connected with a root meaning ‘bend or turn.’"}],"formationLogic":"The eye membrane shares its name with the rainbow; the proposed deeper Greek derivation remains uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The traditional PIE proposal is explicitly marked uncertain.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/iris"},contexts:[{"domain":"Medicine","senseId":"iris.s1","en":"During the examination, the optometrist used a bright lamp to check whether the colored ring of each iris looked healthy and even.","zh":"检查时，验光师用明亮的灯查看每只眼睛虹膜的彩色环是否健康、均匀。","structure":"Used + object + to-infinitive states purpose; whether introduces the indirect question governed by check.","grammar":"iris 在此为眼睛的虹膜；whether 引导宾语从句，looked 后接形容词作表语。","rationale":"The appositive phrase ‘the colored ring’ identifies the eye structure without confusing it with the flower also called an iris.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Bright light caused the iris to contract and let in less light.','强光使虹膜收缩，减少进入眼睛的光线。')],mistakes:[m('The iris is the black opening at the center of the eye that lets light enter.','The pupil is the black opening at the center of the eye that lets light enter.','虹膜是有颜色的环状组织；中央让光线进入的黑色开口叫瞳孔 pupil。')],quiz:[q('iris',1,1,'The iris is the colored ring around the?','pupil of the eye','eyelash on the outer lid','lens inside a camera','iris 指眼睛中有颜色的环状部分。'),q('iris',2,1,'The iris helps control?','how much light enters the eye','how quickly hair grows','the movement of the jaw','虹膜改变瞳孔大小，以调节进入眼睛的光线。'),q('iris',3,1,'Which part is the opening at the center of the iris?','the pupil','the eyelid','the retina’s outer wall','瞳孔是虹膜中央的开口，二者不能混淆。'),q('iris',4,1,'A doctor examining the iris is examining part of the?','eye','ear','digestive tract','iris 是眼睛的组成部分。')]});
D('iron',{etymology:{"origin":"Middle English iron/iren continues Old English iren, from Proto-Germanic *isarn; a deeper Celtic source has been suggested but is not certain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Middle English iron/iren continues Old English iren, from Proto-Germanic *isarn; a deeper Celtic source has been suggested but is not certain."}],"formationLogic":"The word names the metal; its Germanic history is documented, while the still-deeper borrowing proposal is tentative.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The possible Celtic connection is stated only as a suggestion, not as established fact.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/iron"},contexts:[{"domain":"Materials","senseId":"iron.s1","en":"The old gate was made of iron, and despite years of rain it remained strong enough to protect the farm entrance.","zh":"这扇旧门由铁制成，尽管多年淋雨，仍然坚固到足以保护农场入口。","structure":"Be made of + material; despite + noun phrase introduces a contrast, followed by enough + adjective + to-infinitive.","grammar":"iron 作不可数物质名词，表示金属铁；made of 表示材料构成。","rationale":"Rain and strength keep the example centered on iron as a metal, not the appliance or the verb.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The old gate is made of wrought iron.','这扇旧大门是用熟铁制成的。'),ex(2,'Unplug the iron before you leave the room.','离开房间前请拔掉熨斗的插头。'),ex(3,'He selected a nine-iron for the short shot.','这记短击他选了九号铁杆。'),ex(4,'She ironed the shirt before the interview.','面试前她熨平了衬衫。'),ex(5,'The captain showed an iron will during the rescue.','救援过程中，队长表现出了钢铁般的意志。')],mistakes:[m('She ironed the shirt by folding it carefully and never pressing it with a heated iron.','She folded the shirt carefully without ironing it.','iron 作动词表示用熨斗熨平；只折叠而不用熨斗不能称为 ironing。')],quiz:[q('iron',1,1,'Iron is the metal with the chemical symbol?','Fe','H2O','CO2','iron 的化学符号是 Fe。'),q('iron',2,2,'An electric iron is used to?','press clothes smooth','cut cloth into patterns','measure body temperature','iron 作名词也指熨衣服的电器。'),q('iron',3,4,'To iron a shirt is to?','press it with a heated tool to remove creases','wash it with cold water','sew a new collar onto it','iron 作动词表示用熨斗烫平衣物。'),q('iron',4,5,'An iron will describes someone who is?','extremely determined','easily persuaded to quit','made of metal','比喻义 iron 表示坚定、强硬。')]});
D('irony',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin ironia, from Greek eironeia ‘dissimulation, assumed ignorance,’ related to eiron ‘dissembler’; the proposed deeper link is uncertain.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin ironia, from Greek eironeia ‘dissimulation, assumed ignorance,’ related to eiron ‘dissembler’; the proposed deeper link is uncertain."}],"formationLogic":"Irony developed from the idea of feigned ignorance or concealed meaning; the proposed deeper Greek relationship is not certain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The source marks the further Greek etymology as a possibility, so it is not stated as fact.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irony"},contexts:[{"domain":"Conversation","senseId":"irony.s1","en":"When the power failed just as the presentation began, Noah said, “Perfect timing,” using irony to criticize the situation without stating his complaint directly.","zh":"演示刚开始电力就中断，诺亚说“时机真好”，用反语含蓄地表达了对这种情况的不满。","structure":"When-clause sets the occasion; said + quoted words; using-phrase explains the manner and purpose.","grammar":"irony 在此指反语：字面表达与真实态度相反；using 是伴随状语，说明说话方式。","rationale":"The quoted praise is the opposite of Noah's real evaluation, making the verbal-irony sense explicit.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her voice carried a note of irony when she praised the broken printer.','她称赞那台坏掉的打印机时，语气里带着一丝反讽。'),ex(2,'The irony was that the fire station itself had no working alarm.','具有讽刺意味的是，消防站自身竟没有可用的警报器。')],mistakes:[m('She meant exactly what she said and intended no humor or criticism, but her statement was verbal irony.','She meant exactly what she said and described it as a sincere, literal compliment.','真心表达字面赞美并非 verbal irony；反语要求说出的意思与真实意思相反。')],quiz:[q('irony',1,1,'A speaker uses verbal irony when the speaker?','says something opposite to the intended meaning','reads every statement exactly as written','uses a word with no possible meaning','verbal irony 常以反话表达真实意思。'),q('irony',2,2,'The irony of a fire station having no alarm is that?','the situation is the opposite of what people would expect','the station has the newest alarm in town','the alarm was never meant to be used','situational irony 是结果与合理预期相反的讽刺局面。'),q('irony',3,1,'A note of irony in someone’s voice suggests?','a hint of saying one thing while meaning another','a technical error in the sound system','a direct and completely neutral statement','irony 可指语气中的反语或讽刺意味。'),q('irony',4,2,'Which situation is ironic?','A fire station burns down because its alarm failed.','A fire station answers an ordinary emergency call.','A fire station buys a new hose for its trucks.','消防站因警报失灵而失火，结果和预期形成反差。')]});
D('irrational',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin irrationalis, negative in- + rationalis ‘of or belonging to reason’; rationalis is related to ratio ‘reckoning, reason.’","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin irrationalis, negative in- + rationalis ‘of or belonging to reason’; rationalis is related to ratio ‘reckoning, reason.’"}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix reverses rational: an irrational decision is not grounded in reason.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The Latin components are supported by the cited etymological source.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irrational"},contexts:[{"domain":"Decision-making","senseId":"irrational.s1","en":"It was irrational to cancel the entire field study because one sensor failed; the team could have replaced the device and continued with the other measurements.","zh":"仅仅因为一个传感器失灵就取消整个实地研究是不理性的；团队本可以更换设备，继续进行其他测量。","structure":"It + be + adjective + to-infinitive; because-clause gives the reason, and the semicolon adds a more reasoned alternative.","grammar":"irrational 作表语；it 是形式主语，真正主语是 to cancel...。","rationale":"The available alternative shows why the decision lacks reasonable proportion, directly illustrating ‘not based on reason.’","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'His irrational fear of elevators made him climb twelve flights of stairs.','他对电梯毫无理性的恐惧让他爬了十二层楼梯。'),ex(2,'It would be irrational to reject the offer without reading its terms.','不看条款就拒绝这份报价是不理性的。'),ex(3,'The square root of three is irrational.','三的平方根是无理数。')],mistakes:[m('The number 3/2 is irrational because it can be expressed exactly as a ratio of two integers.','The number 3/2 is rational because it can be expressed exactly as a ratio of two integers.','能表示为两个整数之比的数是有理数；3/2 不能称为 irrational。')],quiz:[q('irrational',1,1,'An irrational fear is?','not supported by reason or evidence','carefully based on clear evidence','a type of mathematical fraction','irrational 可指不理性的恐惧。'),q('irrational',2,2,'An irrational decision may seem?','unreasonable or lacking a good basis','fully justified by every fact','unrelated to any choice','irrational 也可表示没有道理、荒谬的。'),q('irrational',3,3,'An irrational number cannot be written as?','a ratio of two integers','a decimal expansion','a symbol in a math book','数学中的 irrational number 不能表示为两个整数之比。'),q('irrational',4,3,'Which is an irrational number?','the square root of 2','3 divided by 2','the integer 7','√2 是无理数，而 3/2 和 7 都是有理数。')]});
D('irregular',{etymology:{"origin":"From Old French irreguler and Medieval Latin irregularis ‘not regular,’ with assimilated negative in- + Latin regularis ‘having rules.’","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Old French irreguler and Medieval Latin irregularis ‘not regular,’ with assimilated negative in- + Latin regularis ‘having rules.’"}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix marks departure from regular form or pattern; here it describes a coastline without an even outline.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The Latin and Old French formation is supported by the etymological source.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irregular"},contexts:[{"domain":"Geography","senseId":"irregular.s1","en":"The island's irregular coastline has narrow bays, sharp inlets, and rocky points, so a straight-line estimate gives a misleading picture of its length.","zh":"这座岛不规则的海岸线有狭窄海湾、尖锐的凹口和岩石岬角，因此直线估算会让人误解其长度。","structure":"Possessive noun phrase + subject + verb; so introduces the consequence of the uneven pattern.","grammar":"irregular 作定语修饰 coastline；这里描述形状不均匀，而非时间间隔或动词变化。","rationale":"The examples of bays, inlets, and points establish the uneven-shape sense, and the final clause shows its effect on measurement.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The coast has an irregular outline with many small bays.','海岸线轮廓不规则，有许多小海湾。'),ex(2,'Because his hours are irregular, he cannot plan dinner at a fixed time.','由于工作时间不规律，他无法安排固定时间吃晚饭。'),ex(3,'Auditors found irregular payments in the company records.','审计人员在公司记录中发现了不合规付款。'),ex(4,'Go is an irregular verb because its past form is went.','go 是不规则动词，因为它的过去式是 went。'),ex(5,'The novel follows a group of irregulars who fight outside the official army.','这部小说讲述一群在正规军体系之外作战的非正规军士兵。')],mistakes:[m('The coastline is irregular, forming a perfect straight line with no bends or bays.','The coastline is regular, forming a perfect straight line with no bends or bays.','笔直且没有弯曲的轮廓并非不规则；将 irregular 换成 regular 才符合描述。')],quiz:[q('irregular',1,1,'An irregular shape is?','uneven and not following a regular pattern','perfectly circular by definition','always made of equal sides','irregular 可形容形状不规则或不平整。'),q('irregular',2,2,'Irregular working hours are hours that?','do not occur on a fixed schedule','begin at precisely the same time every day','are forbidden by every law','irregular 也可表示时间安排不固定。'),q('irregular',3,4,'The verb go is irregular because?','its past tense is went, not goed','it has no meaning in English','it cannot be used in a sentence','语法义 irregular 指词形变化不遵循常规。'),q('irregular',4,5,'In a historical novel, irregulars may be?','soldiers outside the official army','auditors checking company payments','verbs with unusual past forms','irregular 作名词可指非正规军士兵。')]});
D('irregularity',{etymology:{"origin":"From Old French irregularité and Medieval Latin irregularitas, from irregularis ‘not regular’; the noun has been used for a nonconforming condition since the late 16th century.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Old French irregularité and Medieval Latin irregularitas, from irregularis ‘not regular’; the noun has been used for a nonconforming condition since the late 16th century."}],"formationLogic":"The noun names the state or instance of failing to conform to a rule; here the mismatched dates make that deviation identifiable.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The sense of a nonconforming condition is historically attested.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irregularity"},contexts:[{"domain":"Auditing","senseId":"irregularity.s1","en":"The auditor found one irregularity in the travel claim: the receipt listed a hotel stay on a night when the employee's itinerary showed an overnight train.","zh":"审计员在差旅报销中发现一处不合规之处：收据显示员工在某晚住了酒店，但行程单显示那晚乘坐夜车。","structure":"Found + object + colon introduces the specific evidence; when-clause modifies night.","grammar":"irregularity 是可数名词，此处表示一项偏离规则的情况；冒号引出具体内容。","rationale":"The mismatch gives a specific departure from normal procedure, rather than using irregularity vaguely to mean any problem.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The audit found an irregularity in the dates listed on two invoices.','审计发现两张发票所列日期存在一处异常。')],mistakes:[m('The audit reported no irregularities and identified three clear irregularities in the same payments.','The audit found three irregularities in the payments and reported them to the board.','同一报告既说没有任何异常，又说发现了三处明确异常，前后矛盾。')],quiz:[q('irregularity',1,1,'An irregularity in an official record is?','something unusual or not in accordance with the rules','a routine entry made exactly as required','a decorative mark with no information','irregularity 指不规则或不合规之处。'),q('irregularity',2,1,'A financial irregularity might lead auditors to?','look more closely for improper payments','stop checking the accounts forever','assume every record is correct','账目异常会促使审计人员进一步核查。'),q('irregularity',3,1,'Which adjective is irregularity derived from?','irregular','irritable','irreplaceable','irregularity 由 irregular 加后缀构成。'),q('irregularity',4,1,'Several irregularities were found. This means?','more than one unusual or improper detail was found','all details were perfectly standard','no records were examined','复数 irregularities 表示发现了多处异常。')]});
D('irrespective',{etymology:{"origin":"Formed from negative in- + respective, originally ‘regardful’; ‘without taking account of circumstances’ developed by the 1690s, and irrespective of is attested around 1800.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Formed from negative in- + respective, originally ‘regardful’; ‘without taking account of circumstances’ developed by the 1690s, and irrespective of is attested around 1800."}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix reverses ‘regardful’: irrespective of a factor means that factor is not taken into account.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The source supports the shift from the older adjective to its modern irrespective-of use.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irrespective"},contexts:[{"domain":"Policy","senseId":"irrespective.s1","en":"The library offers free membership to local residents, irrespective of their income, because access to public information should not depend on wealth.","zh":"图书馆向当地居民免费开放会员资格，不论他们的收入如何，因为获取公共信息不应取决于财富。","structure":"Main clause + supplementary irrespective-of phrase; because-clause gives the policy rationale.","grammar":"irrespective of + 名词表示“不考虑/不论”；介词 of 后用名词 income。","rationale":"The phrase explicitly removes income as a condition for membership, illustrating the ‘without taking into account’ sense.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The clinic accepts patients irrespective of their ability to pay.','这家诊所接收患者，不论他们是否有支付能力。'),ex(2,'The repair will go ahead irrespective of the weather.','不论天气如何，维修都会继续进行。')],mistakes:[m('All applicants are welcome irrespective the age limit stated on the form.','All applicants are welcome irrespective of the age limit stated on the form.','irrespective 后要接 of，再引出不予考虑的因素。')],quiz:[q('irrespective',1,1,'A service offered irrespective of age is offered?','without considering a person’s age','only to people of one exact age','after the person proves their age','irrespective of age 表示不论年龄。'),q('irrespective',2,2,'They continued irrespective of the cost. They continued?','even though the cost did not change their decision','only if the cost became zero','because they had forgotten the cost','irrespective of 表示不受某因素影响或不把它算在内。'),q('irrespective',3,1,'Which phrase is grammatically complete?','irrespective of the outcome','irrespective the outcome','irrespective from the outcome','标准搭配是 irrespective of。'),q('irrespective',4,2,'The rule applies irrespective of location. It applies?','wherever someone is','only in one named city','only after the location is changed','irrespective of location 表示不论地点。')]});
D('irresponsible',{etymology:{"origin":"Formed in the 1640s from negative in- + responsible; the later sense ‘not acting with a sense of responsibility’ is recorded in the 1680s.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"Formed in the 1640s from negative in- + responsible; the later sense ‘not acting with a sense of responsibility’ is recorded in the 1680s."}],"formationLogic":"The negative prefix reverses responsible: failing to meet the duty to secure the lab is irresponsible.","mnemonic":null,"note":"No unsupported further etymology is added for responsible.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irresponsible"},contexts:[{"domain":"Public safety","senseId":"irresponsible.s1","en":"It would be irresponsible to leave the laboratory unlocked overnight when valuable samples and hazardous chemicals are stored inside.","zh":"实验室里存放着贵重样本和危险化学品，却整夜不锁门，这是不负责任的做法。","structure":"It + would be + adjective + to-infinitive; when-clause provides the relevant circumstance.","grammar":"irresponsible 作表语；it 是形式主语，to leave... 是真正主语。","rationale":"The stored samples and chemicals establish a clear duty to secure the lab, so the judgment is not a vague personal criticism.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'It was irresponsible to leave the laboratory unlocked overnight.','把实验室整夜不锁是不负责任的。')],mistakes:[m('The driver acted irresponsibly by following every safety rule and protecting every passenger; this was responsible behavior.','The driver acted responsibly by following every safety rule and protecting every passenger; this was responsible behavior.','遵守安全规则体现负责，与 irresponsible 评价冲突；改 responsible 才与说明一致。')],quiz:[q('irresponsible',1,1,'An irresponsible choice shows?','a failure to act with proper care','careful attention to one’s duties','a clear plan to protect others','irresponsible 表示不负责任、没有尽到应有责任。'),q('irresponsible',2,1,'Leaving a small child alone near traffic is?','irresponsible','inviolable','invaluable','没有照看孩子使其处于危险中是不负责任的。'),q('irresponsible',3,1,'Which noun means the quality of being irresponsible?','irresponsibility','responsibility','responsibly','irresponsibility 是 irresponsible 的名词形式。'),q('irresponsible',4,1,'Choose the correct sentence.','It was irresponsible to ignore the safety warning.','It was irresponsibility to ignore the safety warningly.','It irresponsible to ignored the safety warning.','常用句式是 It is irresponsible to do something。')]});
D('irrigate',{etymology:{"origin":"From Latin irrigatus, past participle of irrigare ‘lead water to, refresh, irrigate’; in- here means ‘into/on,’ while rigare ‘water, moisten’ has uncertain origin.","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[{"label":"来源与演变","text":"From Latin irrigatus, past participle of irrigare ‘lead water to, refresh, irrigate’; in- here means ‘into/on,’ while rigare ‘water, moisten’ has uncertain origin."}],"formationLogic":"The Latin verb describes directing water onto land; the deeper origin of rigare is uncertain.","mnemonic":null,"note":"The etymological source itself treats the origin of rigare as uncertain.","source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/irrigate"},contexts:[{"domain":"Agriculture","senseId":"irrigate.s1","en":"During the dry month, the cooperative irrigated the young orchards at night, when cooler air reduced water loss from the soil.","zh":"在干旱的月份里，合作社夜间灌溉新果园，此时较凉的空气减少了土壤水分流失。","structure":"Main clause in simple past; when-clause modifies night and gives the reason for choosing that time.","grammar":"irrigate 是及物动词，后接受水灌溉的土地；when 引导时间状语从句。","rationale":"The orchards are the land supplied with water so crops can grow, matching the agricultural sense precisely.","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Canals irrigate the fields during the dry months.','干旱月份，运河为田地灌溉。'),ex(2,'The nurse irrigated the wound with clean saline solution.','护士用干净的生理盐水冲洗伤口。')],mistakes:[m('The nurse irrigated the wound by leaving it covered in dry dust and never using liquid.','The nurse cleaned the wound with saline rather than irrigating it with liquid.','irrigate 身体部位是用液体冲洗；只覆盖干燥灰尘且不用液体不符合这个动作。')],quiz:[q('irrigate',1,1,'Farmers irrigate a field when they?','supply it with water for crops','remove every seed from the soil','cover it with a roof','irrigate 土地指为作物灌溉。'),q('irrigate',2,2,'A nurse irrigates a wound by?','flushing it with a flow of liquid','sewing it shut without cleaning','covering it with dry paper only','医学中 irrigate 可表示用液体冲洗伤口。'),q('irrigate',3,1,'Which phrase fits the agricultural sense?','irrigate the crops','irrigate the harvest into a bag','irrigate the tractor with a plow','irrigate the crops 是农业灌溉搭配。'),q('irrigate',4,2,'Which liquid is appropriate for irrigating a wound in a clinical setting?','sterile saline','dry sand','engine oil','临床冲洗伤口使用适当的无菌液体。')]});
